WEBVTT

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.560
- Wow! It's Mt. Fuji!
- It's so pretty!

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.260
It's definitely the best mountain in Japan!

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.920
What's that?

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:41.400
Oh, those are the new Twin
Tower Buildings in West Tama City.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:48.180
319 meters and 294 meters in height,
and the tallest twins in Japan!

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.350
I wish I could visit!

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:54.180
Doc! Let's stop by on our way
home from camping tomorrow!

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:59.320
Hmm. It's a little out of the way, but sure.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:01.860
West Tama City ...

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:05.190
That's where I exposed
the former mayor's crimes,

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:09.270
and where Moriya Teiji
tried to get the best of me ...

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:14.670
Still, these guys sure love camping ...

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.830
Camp tomorrow! Camp the day after tomorrow!

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:21.600
"Camp Grounds"

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:31.220
Thank you for the food!

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:34.360
Hold on! You still have rice left!

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:38.660
My mom said it's bad luck to
waste even one grain of rice!

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:44.970
That's correct! Rice farmers
work hard 88 times to make rice!

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.540
88 times?

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:47.900
Yes!

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:53.340
If you cut up the character for "rice",
you get "88" out of it, right?

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:54.580
You do?

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.850
- Oh, you do!
- You're right!

00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:00.980
That's why the age of 88
is called the "rice age".

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:04.420
While we're at it, 77 is
called the "happiness age",

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:07.290
and 99 is the "white age".

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:10.390
Do you know why 77 is the "happiness age"?

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:14.300
Because the character for
"happiness" looks like "77" in cursive.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.330
Right?

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:18.930
The "white age" is 99 because
"white" is "100" with one line missing.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:23.440
Wow! You two always know so much!

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:27.610
I bet you guys are
actually lying about your ages!

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:29.350
You got that right ...

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:31.710
So now I have a riddle for you!

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:36.390
Can you guess what age 44 is called?!

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:39.320
44?

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:42.390
Here's a hint! One kanji
and three katakana characters!

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.830
You don't need to add "age" to the end!

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.390
"44"
You don't need to add "age" to the end!

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:47.830
"44"
One kanji and three katakana characters ...

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:49.170
"44"
What could it be?

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:49.700
What could it be?

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:55.500
44... 88... Oh, geez.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.740
Doc, I figured it out, but man, that's stupid.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:01.610
You think so?

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:05.050
How about you, <i>Ai-kun?</i>
Have you figured it out?

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:07.380
- I don't know, either!
- Me neither!

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:08.780
Likewise!

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:14.660
Then here's the answer! 44 is half of 88, right?

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:20.250
88 is "rice." And since this is
half of that, it's "a half bowl of rice"!

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:22.960
Just as I thought ...

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:27.340
What? What's wrong?

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:30.510
A half bowl of rice!
Let's have two each!

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:31.500
Get it?

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:46.320
"Restrooms"

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:45.620
I peed my pants a little ...

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:54.400
Brr!

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.400
It looks like I'll be going

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:59.100
to the Twin Tower Building
in West Tama City tomorrow.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.760
He'll be coming too, of course.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:11.480
Got it, boss! The Twin Tower
Building in West Tama City!

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:18.490
They say that's the closest
place to heaven, as I recall!

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:22.690
Perfect. It's closest to the afterlife.

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:25.350
Let's use it to hold an execution!

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.920
I'm high school detective Kudo Shinichi.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:58.930
I went with old friend and classmate,
Mori Ran, to an amusement park

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:03.470
where I witnessed a suspicious
deal with a man dressed in black!

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.700
I was so absorbed with watching the deal

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:10.940
that I didn't notice a second
man sneak up from behind me!

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:15.780
He forced me to take a poison,
and when I woke up ...

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:18.880
... my body had shrunk!

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:22.420
If they learned Kudo Shinichi was alive,
they might go after me again,

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.520
putting all the people around me in danger!

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:29.330
Per Dr. Agasa's advice,
I decided to conceal my identity.

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:33.360
When Ran asked my name,
I quickly answered, "Edogawa Conan."

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:34.630
To get information on the men,

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:37.960
I wound up living with
Ran and her detective father.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.910
Okay!

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:47.340
I'm Agasa Hiroshi, genius inventor!

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:50.310
Let me use this chance to
introduce my masterpieces!

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:54.350
The Stun-Gun Wristwatch!
The Voice-Changing Bowtie!

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:56.420
The Power-Assisted Kick Shoes!

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:58.920
The Turbo-Engine Skateboard!

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:02.320
And the Criminal Locator Glasses!

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:07.330
One of the lenses has another
new gizmo attached, as well!

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:12.840
Infrared Telescopic Vision!

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:17.370
I made these all for the now-little Shinichi!

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:22.610
He uses these gadgets to
solve cases using <i>Mori-kun's</i> voice

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:24.880
and catch bad guys!

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:26.210
Take this!

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:33.420
Oh, yes! I nearly forgot!

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:38.090
I also invented the Detective
Badges and Wristwatch Flashlights

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:41.830
that he and his classmates use
for their Junior Detective League!

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:47.400
Incidentally, besides me,
there are four others who know who he is.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:51.410
His father and mystery writer, Kudo Yusaku,

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:54.440
his mother and former actress, Kudo Yukiko,

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:57.580
high school detective of
the west, Hattori <i>Heiji-kun,</i>

00:06:57.580 --> 00:07:01.520
and his classmate, Haibara <i>Ai-kun.</i>

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:03.850
Her real name is Miyano Shiho.

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:06.590
She used to work with the men in black,

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:11.730
but after they killed her sister,
she tried to flee the organization.

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:18.500
She took the same poison as Shinichi
and wound up shrinking.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:23.440
The men in black are
relentlessly pursuing Haibara!

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:29.480
And now, unbeknownst to me,
something's about to happen!

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:33.850
Even when I'm small, my mind
remains that of a sharp detective!

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:36.840
There is always only one truth!

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.590
I feel squished in here ...

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:49.160
It's because you're sitting in the back!
You sat in the front last time!

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:52.070
It seemed more fun back here ...

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:54.440
Hey, Conan. Scoot over more.

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:58.610
Sheesh. It's because you ate 5 bowls
of rice first thing in the morning!

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:01.270
Sorry, I gotta scoot over, <i>Ayumi-chan.</i>

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:05.450
Mitsuhiko! Let's play a game!

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:08.120
Then let's play the 30-second game!

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:12.790
You count 30 seconds in your head,
and then stop the stopwatch.

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:15.620
Cool! Let's all play!

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:18.190
I'm busy driving.

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:19.520
I'll pass, too.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:25.770
28. 29. 30!

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:28.930
40 seconds! 10 seconds over!

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:33.910
29. 30!

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:35.610
27 seconds!

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:36.940
So close!

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:40.120
30!

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.520
Yikes!

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:45.490
59 seconds?
Are you sure this thing isn't busted?

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:47.480
I think it might be you, <i>Genta-kun!</i>

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:53.160
28! 29! 30!

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:55.030
30 seconds exactly!

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:58.630
- Wow, <i>Ayumi-chan!</i>
- You must be psychic!

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:01.270
It was just luck ...

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:06.710
Say, Haibara. Who were
you calling so late last night?

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:10.550
I didn't call anyone. Are you sure
you weren't dreaming, <i>Kojima-kun?</i>

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:12.540
Eh? Was I?

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:19.290
It's so tall!

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:22.160
I can't see the top!

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:24.650
It's like it even goes above the clouds!

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:32.870
Is that you, <i>Conan-kun?!</i>

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:35.670
Huh? <i>Ran-neechan!</i> What's going on?

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:38.710
Hey, you! What're you doing here?!

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:41.740
We came to check out the buildings
on our way home from camping.

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:43.740
What about you?

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:48.320
Tokiwa <i>Mio-kun,</i> the owner
of this Twin Tower Building,

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:51.050
was a junior student of
mine in college, you see,

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:55.560
and she specially invited me
for next week's grand opening!

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:56.830
Oh? I never heard about that.

00:09:56.830 --> 00:10:00.930
Right?! He didn't even tell me, either!

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:03.900
He only confessed after I grilled
him about his strange behavior.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:06.600
Confessed?! I wasn't hiding anything!

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:10.970
I get it! You two came to keep an eye on him!

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:15.040
After all, Tokiwa <i>Mio-san</i> is the rich
daughter of the Tokiwa <i>zaibatsu,</i>

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:16.910
and still single!

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:20.580
And since Ran's parents are
currently separated, she's worried!

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:25.750
Excuse me, but might
you be Mori <i>Kogoro-sama?</i>

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:27.090
Yes.

00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:31.030
I'm Sawaguchi, the president's secretary.

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:36.360
She's with guests at the moment,
so I'll show you the showrooms first.

00:10:38.270 --> 00:10:41.240
Building A is entirely for business offices,

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:46.040
and floors 31 and above
are all occupied by Tokiwa.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:48.840
The showrooms are on the 2nd and 3rd floors.

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:51.610
Hey. What kind of company is Tokiwa?

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:53.780
Mostly computer software,

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:57.120
but they do all sorts of computer-related stuff!

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:01.110
Does that mean they got
video games, too?! I can't wait!

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:11.130
Just look at all these interesting things!

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:13.740
Hello, everyone! Welcome!

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:16.140
This is Hara, our managing
director and programmer!

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:17.640
Nice to meet you!

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:20.410
- What is this?
- Is it an arcade machine?

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:21.810
Wanna try it out?

00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:26.110
This uses a computer to predict
what you'll look like in 10 years!

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:30.250
Oh? What you'll look like
in 10 years? That's amazing!

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:31.990
Doc! Let's try it!

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:35.120
Please sit in the seats, then.

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:39.930
I wouldn't wanna see my old
face from 10 years in the future ...

00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:42.590
Are you ready? Here we go!

00:11:56.710 --> 00:12:01.720
Here is how you two will look in 10 years time!

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:04.350
Huh? It's no different at all ...

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:06.760
This machine is broken!

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:09.690
No, it's not.

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:11.850
Check out <i>Ayumi-chan's.</i>

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:19.740
So cute!

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:23.710
You're way cuter than this girl!

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:26.380
Kids don't know
anything about grownup charm!

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:28.710
- Anyways, let's try it, too!
- Yeah!

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:34.220
- Eh?!
- Not good ...

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:36.220
I totally know high-schoolers like this!

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:39.760
Oh! I think you both look nice!

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:40.820
Really?!

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:42.360
Yes!

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.350
You and me are next!

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.800
I totally know old ladies like that!

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:52.070
Oh, shut up.

00:12:52.070 --> 00:12:54.070
So pretty!

00:12:54.070 --> 00:12:56.170
Oh?!

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:58.410
Looks just like Eri when she was young!

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:01.780
- Almost too good for Shinichi!
- Eh?!

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:05.180
It makes me mad to think that
jerk's stringing this girl along!

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:07.950
Don't say that, Sonoko!

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:09.990
Come on, now ...

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:11.890
What?

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:17.360
- Why are you embarrassed?!
- No, it's not like that ...

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:19.930
Next is Conan and Haibara!

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:20.830
Huh?!

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:22.760
Hey! Haibara!

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:24.430
I'm fine.

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:26.070
I'll pass, too.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:28.770
After all, in 10 years, I'll look like Shinichi,

00:13:28.770 --> 00:13:31.940
and Haibara'll look like Miyano Shiho.

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:33.810
Come on, you!

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:37.950
I'm gonna see what kind of
punk you look like in 10 years!

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:39.780
You too, <i>Haibara-san!</i>

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:41.180
Hold on!

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:42.950
Oh, crap!

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:45.280
I wonder what you'll look like, <i>Conan-kun!</i>

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:54.300
Error?! That's strange...

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:55.860
Lucky!

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:59.200
It might mean neither of us
will exist 10 years from now ...

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:06.010
Yes! Certainly!

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:10.280
Everyone! I'll show you to
the party room on the 75th floor!

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:12.910
Please follow me to the elevators ...

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.020
- I'm sorry!
- Not at all ...

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:16.450
There it is!

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:21.220
She was born in the year of the boar,
so she tends to rush recklessly!

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:23.560
Oh, I see! You do that often?

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:37.840
This elevator goes directly to the 75th floor?

00:14:37.840 --> 00:14:43.510
Yes. This elevator is for VIPs,
so it goes directly to the desired floor.

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:47.520
The only place it can be
stopped from the outside

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:50.390
is the concert hall on the 66th floor.

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:52.620
So high up!

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:54.890
What an amazing view!

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:57.220
It's like we're getting closer to heaven!

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:15.500
We're preparing for the grand
opening party, so it's a little crowded.

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:20.150
<i>Mori-senpai!</i>

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:21.880
<i>Tokiwa-kun!</i> It's been a while!

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:24.890
Thank you for coming all this way!

00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:27.390
Yeah, I was planning to come alone, but ...

00:15:27.390 --> 00:15:31.230
I'm his daughter, Ran!
My mother also sends her regards!

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:32.660
Hey now, Ran!

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.060
Let me introduce you!

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:36.200
- My classmate, Suzuki Sonoko!
- Hello!

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.170
- Dr. Agasa, the inventor!
- Hello!

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:42.970
And Edogawa <i>Conan-kun,</i>
Haibara <i>Ai-chan,</i> Yoshida <i>Ayumi-chan...</i>

00:15:42.970 --> 00:15:44.510
...Tsuburaya <i>Mitsuhiko-kun...</i>
- Hello!

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:47.110
...and Kojima <i>Genta-kun!</i>
- Hi.

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:50.410
It's nice to meet you all! I'm Tokiwa Mio.

00:15:50.410 --> 00:15:52.550
Now let me introduce you!

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:58.250
My art instructor and Japanese-style painter,
Kisaragi <i>Hohsui-sensei.</i>

00:15:58.250 --> 00:16:02.990
Kisaragi Hohsui? The one
famous for his Mt. Fuji paintings?

00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:05.590
I know about you, too!

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:08.360
You're Kogoro the
Catnapping Detective, aren't ya?!

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:11.130
That's "Sleeping Kogoro!"

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:13.440
This guy reeks of booze!

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:17.440
This is Oki <i>Iwamatsu-sensei,</i>
a councilman of West Tama City.

00:16:17.440 --> 00:16:22.580
He assisted with the construction
of this building in many ways.

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:28.280
And this is Kazama <i>Hidehiko-san,</i>
the architect of these buildings!

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:32.950
I have a small connection to you, <i>Mori-san.</i>

00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:37.090
I'm actually a pupil of Moriya Teiji.

00:16:37.090 --> 00:16:38.630
Moriya Teiji?!

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:40.630
But there's no need to worry.

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:44.400
I won't blow up these buildings like Moriya.

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:47.040
B-Blow up?

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:51.010
Because they're different
heights and unsymmetrical, right?

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:53.340
Oh? You know a lot, little boy.

00:16:56.410 --> 00:17:00.150
Hurry! Hurry! You can see it so close up!

00:17:00.150 --> 00:17:02.140
- It's so pretty!
- It's huge!

00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:11.630
Oh! This is an incredible view!

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:15.130
You can even see Fuji at night here.

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:16.400
Even at night?

00:17:16.400 --> 00:17:19.170
What does that mean?

00:17:19.170 --> 00:17:21.660
What can you see from the other side?!

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:29.210
- What's that?
- It looks like a dome roof ...

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:31.550
Tower B is for commerce.

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:36.120
The lower area is for shops,
and the upper area is a hotel.

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:39.020
There's an indoor pool on the top floor,

00:17:39.020 --> 00:17:41.760
and the dome can open and close!

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:44.030
Wow! That's really something!

00:17:44.030 --> 00:17:49.060
Say, <i>Mio-kun.</i> Could you let me
stay in the hotel this weekend?

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:51.200
But we still haven't opened ...

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:53.470
No, in other words?!

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:59.140
Very well. I'll prepare
a suite on the 67th floor.

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:03.780
I'd like to have dinner
with you too, if possible ...

00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:07.480
That's a strange brooch.

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:09.650
A present from someone nice?

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:13.190
No, I got it for myself.

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:16.090
<i>Mio-kun!</i> I'll be leaving now!

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:17.690
Oh, I'll accompany you!

00:18:17.690 --> 00:18:19.680
You needn't see me off!

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:25.170
He seems angry about something ...

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:29.200
<i>Mio-san</i> bought up all of his
paintings and then sold them for a lot.

00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:31.200
He wasn't happy about that ...

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:38.910
Chocolate!

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:45.250
Oh, you caught me! I'll let you have some, too!

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:47.260
Yay!

00:18:47.260 --> 00:18:49.260
- Here you are!
- Thank you!

00:18:49.260 --> 00:18:52.090
- Thank you!
- Thanks!

00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:55.830
He's a brilliant programmer,
but also very childish ...

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:59.230
Oh, but that's how he can make fun games!

00:18:59.230 --> 00:19:00.270
Oh, yes!

00:19:00.270 --> 00:19:06.170
I'm working on a new video game;
could I ask for your opinions?

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:08.380
- For a game?!
- Certainly!

00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:11.150
I live in Soho.

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:12.850
We live in Beika!

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:15.720
That's not far, then! Just a quick bus ride!

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:18.290
Want to come by next Sunday?!

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:21.790
Yes! We'll be there!

00:19:21.790 --> 00:19:23.560
What's wrong, <i>Ai-chan?</i>

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:24.890
Nothing.

00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:33.230
<i>Ran-san.</i>

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:37.270
There's something I'd like
to talk to you about alone.

00:19:37.270 --> 00:19:39.570
Could we meet tomorrow?

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:41.580
Sure, that's fine.

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:44.240
I'll let you know the time and place later.

00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:49.280
<i>Ran-oneesan.</i>

00:19:49.280 --> 00:19:51.550
There's something I
wanna talk to you about alone.

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:52.880
Eh?

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:59.020
It's the hair. That's the problem ...

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:04.790
Maybe I'll try a wave, too!

00:20:07.300 --> 00:20:10.840
Never thought I'd see a
car like that these days!

00:20:10.840 --> 00:20:14.310
- What was it again?
- A Porsche 356A!

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:15.380
What?!

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:19.210
Hold it! That elevator is for VIPs only!

00:20:19.210 --> 00:20:21.680
Employees use the general elevators!

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:24.250
- Y-Yes, ma'am!
- Our apologies!

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:27.560
Tell me! Where did you see
that car?! What color was it?!

00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:31.890
Oh, it was stopped in front
of this building. It was black.

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:33.880
It's Gin's car!

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:38.330
Wait, Conan-kun...!

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:40.320
Hey! Where are you going?!

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:51.970
Hurry! Hurry!

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:56.010
There it is!

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:09.600
Damn!

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:12.930
But ... why'd they come to this building?!

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:33.990
The truth is, I've always liked
<i>Ayumi-chan</i> since kindergarten.

00:21:33.990 --> 00:21:38.360
But she seems to like <i>Conan-kun ...</i>

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:40.360
Please tell me, <i>Ran-san!</i>

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:41.530
How can we go

00:21:41.530 --> 00:21:45.500
from childhood friends to
lovers like you and <i>Shinichi-san?</i>

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:49.500
H-Hold on! Shinichi and I aren't like that!

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:55.340
And, I've started to notice
<i>Haibara-san</i> lately, too ...

00:21:55.340 --> 00:22:00.340
Am I a horrible man to be
fond of two girls at once?!

00:22:06.320 --> 00:22:11.030
It's not horrible at all!
Liking someone is a very good thing,

00:22:11.030 --> 00:22:14.360
and I think you should treasure such feelings!

00:22:14.360 --> 00:22:15.500
Then?!

00:22:15.500 --> 00:22:18.700
But maybe you should just
be close friends for right now?

00:22:18.700 --> 00:22:20.740
With <i>Ayumi-chan</i> and <i>Ai-chan,</i>

00:22:20.740 --> 00:22:24.710
and <i>Conan-kun</i> and <i>Genta-kun</i> too, of course!

00:22:24.710 --> 00:22:26.570
I understand!

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:29.640
Half off five donuts!

00:22:29.640 --> 00:22:31.050
Welcome!

00:22:31.050 --> 00:22:35.320
I really like <i>Conan-kun.</i>

00:22:35.320 --> 00:22:38.320
But he likes someone else.

00:22:38.320 --> 00:22:40.590
Do you mean <i>Ai-chan?</i>

00:22:40.590 --> 00:22:43.530
No. You, <i>Ran-oneesan!</i>

00:22:43.530 --> 00:22:45.360
Don't be silly!

00:22:45.360 --> 00:22:49.060
<i>Conan-kun</i> likes you! I know it!

00:22:49.060 --> 00:22:55.470
So I'd like you to tell him
you already have <i>Shinichi-san</i>

00:22:55.470 --> 00:22:57.940
so he should give up!

00:22:57.940 --> 00:23:00.380
U-Uhh ...

00:23:00.380 --> 00:23:03.440
Otherwise, I'll feel so bad for him ...

00:23:03.440 --> 00:23:07.520
But we don't know for sure
that <i>Conan-kun</i> likes me ...

00:23:07.520 --> 00:23:09.380
I do!

00:23:09.380 --> 00:23:10.520
How?

00:23:10.520 --> 00:23:13.420
My woman's sixth sense!

00:23:13.420 --> 00:23:14.750
O-Oh ...

00:23:18.860 --> 00:23:20.800
Huh? What?!

00:23:20.800 --> 00:23:24.900
I'm telling you, I think
<i>Conan-kun</i> has a crush on me!

00:23:24.900 --> 00:23:28.700
What?! He does not! Don't be stupid!

00:23:28.700 --> 00:23:32.010
Oh? And how do you know that?

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:38.480
No, uhh, childhood love is like the
measles! There's no need to worry!

00:23:38.480 --> 00:23:41.350
Come on, now! Think seriously!

00:23:44.050 --> 00:23:48.560
In that case, don't make any strange lies,
and be honest with yourself.

00:23:48.560 --> 00:23:50.930
Be honest with myself?

00:23:50.930 --> 00:23:55.530
If you do that, the answer
should turn up on its own.

00:23:55.530 --> 00:23:57.520
See ya! I'll call later!

00:24:05.140 --> 00:24:09.470
I'm the one who needs to be honest ...

00:24:21.760 --> 00:24:23.750
W-What are you doing?!

00:24:32.430 --> 00:24:35.570
I've asked you here for but one reason.

00:24:35.570 --> 00:24:38.570
The truth is, a man was found stabbed to death

00:24:38.570 --> 00:24:40.540
in a suite in the Twin Tower Building.

00:24:40.540 --> 00:24:42.180
- Eh?!
- That's!

00:24:42.180 --> 00:24:45.450
Oki Iwamatsu, the West Tama City councilman!

00:24:45.450 --> 00:24:51.490
I hear you were there when he
asked Tokiwa <i>Mio-san</i> for a room.

00:24:51.490 --> 00:24:53.450
- <i>Chiba-kun.</i>
- Yes, sir.

00:24:53.450 --> 00:24:58.630
Mr. Oki's estimated time of death
is between 10:00 PM and midnight.

00:24:58.630 --> 00:25:02.560
We believe a knife was used,
but it wasn't at the scene.

00:25:02.560 --> 00:25:07.200
But there was an <i>"O-choko"</i> cup
by Mr. Oki's hand, split in two.

00:25:07.200 --> 00:25:08.540
<i>O-choko?</i>

00:25:08.540 --> 00:25:09.570
This.

00:25:09.570 --> 00:25:12.470
This <i>O-choko</i> is quite expensive.

00:25:12.470 --> 00:25:17.510
There's a good chance Mr. Oki,
fond of sake, brought it with him,

00:25:17.510 --> 00:25:21.980
and that it's a dying message
indicating who the killer is.

00:25:21.980 --> 00:25:28.660
In other words, the police think the
suspect is one of those five people?

00:25:28.660 --> 00:25:35.100
The building still hasn't been
opened to the public, you see.

00:25:35.100 --> 00:25:40.770
Oh! I got it! The <i>"O-choko"</i>
refers to "chocolate"!

00:25:40.770 --> 00:25:44.570
The killer was the
chocolate-loving Hara Yoshiaki!

00:25:44.570 --> 00:25:45.940
- Eh?!
- No way!

00:25:45.940 --> 00:25:47.840
It wasn't <i>Hara-san!</i>

00:25:47.840 --> 00:25:52.050
He's a nice person!
He shared his chocolate with us!

00:25:52.050 --> 00:25:52.810
Yeah!

00:25:52.810 --> 00:25:54.850
Hey! Quiet, you!

00:25:54.850 --> 00:25:58.020
<i>Hara-san</i> is most likely in the clear.

00:25:58.020 --> 00:26:02.590
Of the five people we questioned,
he was the only one with an alibi.

00:26:02.590 --> 00:26:04.660
Alibi?

00:26:04.660 --> 00:26:09.000
That's not nice, Inspector!
You should've said so at the start!

00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:11.870
Could <i>"O-choko"</i> refer
to <i>"ochokochoi"?</i> [clumsy]

00:26:11.870 --> 00:26:15.640
If so, then <i>Mori-san</i> would
be the most suspicious of all.

00:26:15.640 --> 00:26:17.540
Hold on, Shiratori!

00:26:17.540 --> 00:26:19.170
It's a joke.

00:26:19.170 --> 00:26:20.840
Honestly, now ...

00:26:20.840 --> 00:26:23.080
What about motive?

00:26:23.080 --> 00:26:25.210
We're investigating that as we speak.

00:26:25.210 --> 00:26:31.650
Although a councilman, Mr. Oki
held more sway than the mayor.

00:26:31.650 --> 00:26:37.230
Supposedly, he even forced
the revision of a city ordinance

00:26:37.230 --> 00:26:39.890
preventing skyscrapers
from being built in the area.

00:26:39.890 --> 00:26:41.900
So that's why <i>Mio-san</i> couldn't say no

00:26:41.900 --> 00:26:46.730
when <i>Oki-san</i> asked for a hotel
room before the grand opening.

00:26:46.730 --> 00:26:50.910
Come to think of it, the brooch she had on

00:26:50.910 --> 00:26:53.310
looked like that broken <i>O-choko.</i>

00:26:53.310 --> 00:26:56.010
Just a minute! <i>Mio-kun</i> couldn't have...!

00:26:56.010 --> 00:27:01.680
No. It would've been the
easiest for her to commit the crime.

00:27:01.680 --> 00:27:06.590
After all, she lives on
the 68th floor of Tower B,

00:27:06.590 --> 00:27:09.860
one floor above the room he was staying in.

00:27:09.860 --> 00:27:12.190
B-But ...

00:27:12.190 --> 00:27:14.600
Say. Doesn't that <i>O-choko</i>
look like the small bowl used

00:27:14.600 --> 00:27:18.030
when doing Japanese-style paintings?

00:27:18.030 --> 00:27:21.140
My daddy does
Japanese-style paintings as a hobby.

00:27:21.140 --> 00:27:26.010
It reminds me of a mortar
used to grind the powder!

00:27:26.010 --> 00:27:29.210
So the <i>O-choko</i> links to Mr. Kisaragi ...

00:27:29.210 --> 00:27:35.780
But it doesn't seem to link to
<i>Sawaguchi-san</i> or <i>Kazama-san ...</i>

00:27:35.780 --> 00:27:40.960
Shiratori-san, is it true
<i>Kazama-san</i> is Moriya Teiji's pupil?

00:27:40.960 --> 00:27:42.290
It's true.

00:27:42.290 --> 00:27:47.030
But he's more of the technical
type than the artistic Moriya,

00:27:47.030 --> 00:27:49.260
so he doesn't have a preferred style.

00:27:49.260 --> 00:27:53.700
As for Sawaguchi <i>Chinami-san,</i>
her father was a newspaper reporter,

00:27:53.700 --> 00:27:57.310
and he died from overwork when
she was in her 4th year in college.

00:27:57.310 --> 00:28:00.810
But we've yet to find a
connection between him and Mr. Oki.

00:28:00.810 --> 00:28:02.140
Inspector.

00:28:02.140 --> 00:28:06.310
In my opinion, this incident
was meant to disrupt the ...

00:28:06.310 --> 00:28:09.680
Only the lower part of the
closet has blood splatters ...

00:28:09.680 --> 00:28:12.350
And it's in a strange shape ...

00:28:13.650 --> 00:28:16.120
That isn't for a child's eyes.

00:28:16.120 --> 00:28:18.660
Sorry ...

00:28:18.660 --> 00:28:23.400
Still, what were Gin and Vodka
doing at the Twin Tower Building?

00:28:23.400 --> 00:28:24.800
Wait!

00:28:24.800 --> 00:28:28.440
O-choko cups are for holding alcohol!

00:28:28.440 --> 00:28:33.040
Hey, Haibara. Could it have been them?!

00:28:33.040 --> 00:28:36.010
It's true that they have alcohol codenames.

00:28:36.010 --> 00:28:41.350
But they'd never be foolish enough
to leave such an obvious message.

00:28:44.120 --> 00:28:46.110
... as possible. Got it?

00:28:55.800 --> 00:28:57.830
<i>Mitsuhiko-kun!</i> Over here!

00:28:57.830 --> 00:28:59.870
You two are early!

00:28:59.870 --> 00:29:01.300
This is too exciting!

00:29:01.300 --> 00:29:04.740
I'm so happy to think we'll
beat Conan to the punch!

00:29:04.740 --> 00:29:06.730
Who are you beating to the punch?

00:29:13.180 --> 00:29:15.050
How did you know?!

00:29:15.050 --> 00:29:18.950
You guys are always so predictable!

00:29:18.950 --> 00:29:23.390
You thought I'd stop you from
investigating the case yourselves

00:29:23.390 --> 00:29:25.260
because it's too dangerous, right?

00:29:25.260 --> 00:29:27.250
B-Bingo!

00:29:33.940 --> 00:29:37.910
It's too late this time, but don't
do stuff on your own anymore!

00:29:37.910 --> 00:29:39.770
Okay!

00:29:39.770 --> 00:29:42.880
Do these guys really understand anything?

00:29:42.880 --> 00:29:45.750
So? Who're we seeing today?

00:29:45.750 --> 00:29:49.420
<i>Kazama-san</i> and <i>Kisaragi-san!</i>
And tomorrow is <i>Hara-san!</i>

00:29:49.420 --> 00:29:52.250
<i>Kazama-san</i> lives in Setagaya,

00:29:52.250 --> 00:29:56.820
but he has a workroom in Asahino,
just before West Tama City!

00:29:56.820 --> 00:29:59.760
He's staying there until
the building's grand opening!

00:29:59.760 --> 00:30:01.400
<i>Kisaragi-san</i> is single

00:30:01.400 --> 00:30:05.930
and built a house in Asahino
with a studio three years ago!

00:30:05.930 --> 00:30:09.400
Wow. They really did their homework.

00:30:09.400 --> 00:30:13.070
It's too bad <i>Haibara-san</i> didn't
come too, since we're all going!

00:30:13.070 --> 00:30:15.380
Huh? You invited her, too?

00:30:15.380 --> 00:30:16.310
Yes!

00:30:16.310 --> 00:30:20.300
But she said she was
busy cleaning house today!

00:30:34.560 --> 00:30:36.800
Brother!

00:30:36.800 --> 00:30:42.400
I guess this is what traitors get ...

00:30:42.400 --> 00:30:46.240
Brother! Brother!

00:30:52.810 --> 00:30:57.850
I believe <i>Kazama-san's</i>
apartment is right by the station.

00:30:57.850 --> 00:30:59.820
And <i>Kisaragi-san's</i> house is ...

00:30:59.820 --> 00:31:03.260
Yeah! Up on that hill!

00:31:03.260 --> 00:31:06.590
Let's go see <i>Kazama-san</i> first!

00:31:14.100 --> 00:31:17.140
Wow! This is a CAD system, right?

00:31:17.140 --> 00:31:19.840
Blueprints are all done on computer, right?

00:31:19.840 --> 00:31:22.910
Oh! You know a lot!

00:31:22.910 --> 00:31:26.210
No one uses drafting boards these days.

00:31:26.210 --> 00:31:29.450
What's a drafting board?

00:31:29.450 --> 00:31:32.990
I see! You've actually never heard of them?

00:31:32.990 --> 00:31:36.320
In the old days, you'd put a
piece of paper on a big board

00:31:36.320 --> 00:31:38.890
and draw with a pencil and ruler.

00:31:38.890 --> 00:31:41.000
Oh? Really?

00:31:41.000 --> 00:31:44.130
So, do you kids need something?

00:31:44.130 --> 00:31:46.000
C'mon! Hurry and ask!

00:31:46.000 --> 00:31:50.200
- M-Me?
- You suggested this!

00:31:50.200 --> 00:31:52.870
Fine.

00:31:52.870 --> 00:31:56.540
Actually, <i>Kazama-san!</i> We ...

00:31:56.540 --> 00:32:00.010
... think this is a nice place you have here!

00:32:00.010 --> 00:32:03.880
You have fresh air, and you can see Mt. Fuji!

00:32:03.880 --> 00:32:05.120
Oh, geez.

00:32:05.120 --> 00:32:07.620
We're the Junior Detective League!

00:32:07.620 --> 00:32:09.090
Eh?

00:32:09.090 --> 00:32:12.420
We're investigating <i>Oki-san's</i> murder!

00:32:14.330 --> 00:32:16.530
That's reassuring to hear!

00:32:16.530 --> 00:32:22.570
Sure! Ask anything you want, little detectives!

00:32:22.570 --> 00:32:27.580
Okay, then. What was your
opinion of the late <i>Oki-san?</i>

00:32:27.580 --> 00:32:30.240
Right off the bat, I see.

00:32:30.240 --> 00:32:32.550
A rude old man, I suppose.

00:32:32.550 --> 00:32:37.250
But I got this job because he
revised the city building ordinance,

00:32:37.250 --> 00:32:39.520
so in that sense, I'm thankful to him.

00:32:39.520 --> 00:32:44.690
Did you argue with him about
anything during the drafting stage?

00:32:44.690 --> 00:32:46.930
Nothing with <i>Oki-san...</i>

00:32:46.930 --> 00:32:49.000
You argued with someone else, then?

00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:52.330
Eh? No, that's not what I meant ...

00:32:54.970 --> 00:32:57.240
Oh? That photo ...

00:32:57.240 --> 00:33:02.040
Oh. He's my son. Cute, isn't he?

00:33:02.040 --> 00:33:06.980
I really miss his voice when
I'm working alone at night.

00:33:06.980 --> 00:33:11.320
I sometimes call when I know
he's asleep. I'm such a doting father!

00:33:23.060 --> 00:33:24.390
C'mon ...

00:33:27.200 --> 00:33:31.190
Umm, we're the Junior Detective League ...

00:33:34.310 --> 00:33:36.510
We're investigating <i>Oki-san's ...</i>

00:33:36.510 --> 00:33:40.480
Children have no place
acting like the authorities!

00:33:40.480 --> 00:33:42.140
No, uhh...!

00:33:45.320 --> 00:33:49.020
But it would be a shame
to leave empty-handed.

00:33:49.020 --> 00:33:51.510
I'll give you something nice as souvenirs.

00:33:57.460 --> 00:34:00.000
I appreciate the drawing, but ...

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:02.340
We didn't get to ask about the incident.

00:34:02.340 --> 00:34:05.510
I guess the police should handle it, huh?

00:34:05.510 --> 00:34:08.110
Exactly.

00:34:08.110 --> 00:34:10.100
It's 6:00. Let's head home now.

00:34:22.420 --> 00:34:25.290
W-What was that sound?!

00:34:25.290 --> 00:34:27.620
Oh, just me snoring?

00:34:42.110 --> 00:34:44.110
Haibara was on the phone
in the middle of the night?

00:34:44.110 --> 00:34:48.650
Remember what <i>Genta-kun</i>
said when we went camping?

00:34:48.650 --> 00:34:52.490
I guess she really was on the phone ...

00:34:52.490 --> 00:34:56.590
But she has no one to call, right?

00:34:56.590 --> 00:34:59.060
I trust her.

00:34:59.060 --> 00:35:03.330
But there is a small chance
that her fear of the men in black

00:35:03.330 --> 00:35:06.320
could've made her join
the organization again ...

00:35:08.170 --> 00:35:11.500
It's okay, Doc. There's no need to worry. Later!

00:35:17.110 --> 00:35:19.080
Hey! You're all early!

00:35:19.080 --> 00:35:20.250
Good morning, <i>Conan-kun!</i>

00:35:20.250 --> 00:35:23.080
- What took so long?!
- We've been waiting!

00:35:23.080 --> 00:35:25.490
<i>Haibara-san</i> wants to visit <i>Hara-san,</i> too!

00:35:25.490 --> 00:35:28.090
Eh? Oh.

00:35:28.090 --> 00:35:33.750
What's wrong with that?
I'm interested in his video games, too.

00:35:41.140 --> 00:35:45.130
Room 407. This is <i>Hara-san's</i> apartment!

00:35:47.610 --> 00:35:50.710
Huh? The door's open ...

00:35:50.710 --> 00:35:53.110
That's careless of him!

00:35:53.110 --> 00:35:55.100
<i>Hara-san!</i> We're here!

00:35:57.750 --> 00:36:00.410
<i>C-Conan-kun! Hara-san</i> is!

00:36:02.160 --> 00:36:03.820
Police and ambulance!

00:36:10.130 --> 00:36:13.770
He was shot in the chest!
He died almost instantly!

00:36:13.770 --> 00:36:16.200
A knife?!

00:36:16.200 --> 00:36:18.190
He was about to have cake?

00:36:20.840 --> 00:36:23.880
An O-choko cup!

00:36:23.880 --> 00:36:26.370
Which means it was the same killer!

00:36:33.450 --> 00:36:35.490
Well, Examiner?

00:36:35.490 --> 00:36:39.190
We'll need to do an autopsy to be sure,

00:36:39.190 --> 00:36:44.160
but he died between yesterday
afternoon and yesterday evening.

00:36:44.160 --> 00:36:48.170
It appears he was about to
have some chocolate cake.

00:36:48.170 --> 00:36:54.680
Then, when the killer entered,
he tried to fight with his silver knife ...

00:36:54.680 --> 00:36:59.180
But what should we think
about this <i>O-choko</i> cup?

00:36:59.180 --> 00:37:04.250
Isn't it obvious? It's a serial
murder committed by Mr. Oki's killer.

00:37:04.250 --> 00:37:09.690
It's now likely the <i>O-choko</i> cups
are not the victims dying messages,

00:37:09.690 --> 00:37:12.860
but rather messages from the killer.

00:37:12.860 --> 00:37:14.630
Hey there, kid!

00:37:14.630 --> 00:37:16.630
Are you done already, <i>Tome-san?</i>

00:37:16.630 --> 00:37:20.800
Yeah. Say, I hear you
were the ones who found him?

00:37:20.800 --> 00:37:23.270
Yeah. It was a shock.

00:37:23.270 --> 00:37:25.210
Oh, is that the <i>O-choko</i> cup?

00:37:25.210 --> 00:37:26.640
That's right.

00:37:26.640 --> 00:37:28.970
<i>Huh? There's no blood on it.</i>

00:37:31.250 --> 00:37:33.850
Say, <i>Tome-san.</i> Is that all of the cup?

00:37:33.850 --> 00:37:37.750
Of course! Nothing escapes Tome the Examiner!

00:37:37.750 --> 00:37:39.220
Bye, now!

00:37:39.220 --> 00:37:44.210
Now is it clear it's not them?
They'd never leave those behind.

00:37:50.260 --> 00:37:54.000
After conducting an autopsy,
we know his approximate time of death.

00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:56.670
Yesterday evening, between 5:00 and 6:00.

00:37:56.670 --> 00:38:01.740
Also, all of Mr. Hara's
computer data had been erased.

00:38:01.740 --> 00:38:05.250
It's possible that was the motive.

00:38:05.250 --> 00:38:07.750
Mr. Kisaragi was with
<i>Conan-kun</i> and his friends

00:38:07.750 --> 00:38:10.420
between 5:00 and 6:00, so he's in the clear.

00:38:10.420 --> 00:38:14.790
On the other hand, Mr. Kazama
could've driven there in time

00:38:14.790 --> 00:38:16.890
after <i>Conan-kun</i> and the others left.

00:38:16.890 --> 00:38:19.260
What about <i>Mio-kun?</i>

00:38:19.260 --> 00:38:23.360
Neither <i>Tokiwa-san</i> nor
<i>Sawaguchi-san</i> has a clear alibi.

00:38:23.360 --> 00:38:26.270
I'm sorry, <i>Mori-kun,</i> but I think the killer is

00:38:26.270 --> 00:38:32.270
Tokiwa <i>Mio-san,</i> Kazama Hidehiko,
or Sawaguchi <i>Chinami-san.</i>

00:38:32.270 --> 00:38:36.880
And it's very possible that
these incidents will continue.

00:38:36.880 --> 00:38:43.020
So Inspector Megure suggested
postponing the party this Saturday,

00:38:43.020 --> 00:38:44.820
but she wouldn't listen.

00:38:44.820 --> 00:38:47.810
Not only that, she gave me this to give to you.

00:38:51.630 --> 00:38:54.360
This is an invitation to the party ...

00:38:54.360 --> 00:38:58.970
And <i>Conan-kun,</i> the children,
and I are all listed, too!

00:38:58.970 --> 00:39:00.770
Eh?! Us too?!

00:39:00.770 --> 00:39:04.100
Honestly! What is she thinking?

00:39:31.630 --> 00:39:33.470
Boss!

00:39:33.470 --> 00:39:34.940
This the place?

00:39:34.940 --> 00:39:38.840
The manager confirmed her picture.

00:39:38.840 --> 00:39:44.380
To think she holed up in this dump
to hide from the organization ...

00:39:44.380 --> 00:39:46.910
The rent was paid an entire year in advance,

00:39:46.910 --> 00:39:49.350
and nobody ever answers the phone.

00:39:49.350 --> 00:39:55.120
The neighbors say messages
get left on it sometimes,

00:39:55.120 --> 00:39:59.030
but strangely enough,
when I checked the machine ...

00:39:59.030 --> 00:40:02.030
... There were no messages recorded.

00:40:02.030 --> 00:40:07.670
Eh?! Y-Yes. What's that all about?

00:40:07.670 --> 00:40:11.540
Women will be women.

00:40:11.540 --> 00:40:16.010
There's a computer in the car. Go get it.

00:40:16.010 --> 00:40:19.380
The organization's phone-tracing program.

00:40:19.380 --> 00:40:23.680
With this, we can trace calls in 20 seconds.

00:40:23.680 --> 00:40:25.020
Gotcha!

00:41:08.100 --> 00:41:11.970
Hello, this is Miyano. I'm not home right now.

00:41:11.970 --> 00:41:15.960
Please leave your name
and message after the beep.

00:41:17.740 --> 00:41:20.810
Sister? It's me.

00:41:20.810 --> 00:41:24.800
I'm going to the Twin Tower
Building's opening party ...

00:41:25.710 --> 00:41:27.540
"Unable to trace"

00:41:31.990 --> 00:41:33.890
<i>Kudo-kun...</i>

00:41:33.890 --> 00:41:36.960
So you were calling your sister.

00:41:36.960 --> 00:41:42.460
The phone in the apartment
she used when she was alive.

00:41:42.460 --> 00:41:46.800
Now I see! You wanted
to talk to your late sister.

00:41:49.500 --> 00:41:52.240
I can imagine how you feel,
but it's too dangerous ...

00:41:52.240 --> 00:41:54.900
No one knows how I feel!

00:41:56.780 --> 00:41:59.680
- Hey, Haibara!
- Hold on!

00:41:59.680 --> 00:42:01.670
Let her be for now.

00:42:17.800 --> 00:42:22.840
Damn! Just a few more
seconds and we would've had it!

00:42:22.840 --> 00:42:23.800
Boss!

00:42:23.800 --> 00:42:29.610
Hello, this is Miyano. I'm not
home right now. Please leave ...

00:42:29.610 --> 00:42:31.780
She erased the message!

00:42:31.780 --> 00:42:35.720
You don't think she knows we're here, do you?!

00:42:35.720 --> 00:42:42.560
No, that's not it. She erased the
message so no one will hear it later.

00:42:42.560 --> 00:42:45.530
Never in her dreams would she
think we're sitting next to the phone,

00:42:45.530 --> 00:42:48.830
listening in on her.

00:42:48.830 --> 00:42:51.360
Think she'll call again?

00:42:51.360 --> 00:42:53.900
I doubt it.

00:42:53.900 --> 00:42:59.570
But it sounds like the heavens
are offering us their support!

00:42:59.570 --> 00:43:02.240
The Twin Tower Building's opening party ...

00:43:05.580 --> 00:43:09.220
I'll finally get to see it, Sherry.

00:43:09.220 --> 00:43:12.880
Your cold, dead face...

00:43:27.800 --> 00:43:30.300
I'm sorry about last night.

00:43:30.300 --> 00:43:37.580
I knew it was dangerous, too.
I knew I had to stop at some point.

00:43:37.580 --> 00:43:42.920
Even so, whenever I would
feel especially alone or afraid,

00:43:42.920 --> 00:43:45.750
I would pick up the phone without thinking ...

00:43:45.750 --> 00:43:49.760
Just to hear those 10 seconds
of my sister's voice ...

00:43:49.760 --> 00:43:52.750
Don't be stupid. You're not alone.

00:43:56.630 --> 00:44:01.740
I figured it was about time
to call it quits, so I'll stop.

00:44:01.740 --> 00:44:04.570
Don't worry. I deleted the message.

00:44:07.740 --> 00:44:12.080
But lately, I wonder who I am ...

00:44:14.920 --> 00:44:20.150
I wonder who I am, and where I belong ...

00:44:20.150 --> 00:44:23.060
I have no place to be.

00:44:23.060 --> 00:44:25.930
Eh?! You have no place?!

00:44:25.930 --> 00:44:27.790
What're you talking about, Haibara?

00:44:27.790 --> 00:44:31.930
You have a seat right there!

00:44:31.930 --> 00:44:33.670
This is mine!

00:44:33.670 --> 00:44:35.140
This is my place!

00:44:35.140 --> 00:44:37.130
And this is mine!

00:44:39.170 --> 00:44:42.160
See? I told you you're not alone.

00:44:51.050 --> 00:44:52.880
"Central Surveillance Room"

00:45:25.220 --> 00:45:29.020
C'mon! Where's the spoiled rich girl?!

00:45:29.020 --> 00:45:30.820
She said she's on her way.

00:45:30.820 --> 00:45:32.690
I can't wait for the party!

00:45:32.690 --> 00:45:36.800
- I bet there'll be a lot of food!
- I want boxed eel lunches!

00:45:36.800 --> 00:45:39.800
I don't think they'll have that.

00:45:39.800 --> 00:45:42.700
Say. Do you think <i>Hara-san,</i>
the managing director,

00:45:42.700 --> 00:45:46.740
could've been working with the men in black?

00:45:46.740 --> 00:45:48.840
It's possible.

00:45:48.840 --> 00:45:51.710
They've been bringing in
promising young people from all fields,

00:45:51.710 --> 00:45:55.720
including politicians, businessmen,
doctors, scientists, and more.

00:45:55.720 --> 00:45:57.450
Even Councilman Oki?

00:45:57.450 --> 00:46:01.020
He didn't have much power,
but maybe when he was younger.

00:46:01.020 --> 00:46:04.160
In any case, once inside the organization,

00:46:04.160 --> 00:46:10.230
whoever tries to leave or betray
it can expect a death sentence.

00:46:10.230 --> 00:46:12.900
Just like how they're trying to kill me.

00:46:12.900 --> 00:46:17.270
In which case,
if the killer is one of those four ...

00:46:17.270 --> 00:46:18.070
Yeah.

00:46:18.070 --> 00:46:22.080
There's a good chance they're
connected with the organization, too.

00:46:22.080 --> 00:46:24.880
Hi! Sorry for the wait!

00:46:24.880 --> 00:46:27.910
Sonoko! What happened to your hair?!

00:46:27.910 --> 00:46:30.850
It's an image change!

00:46:30.850 --> 00:46:34.090
I decided to take after her and try a wave!

00:46:34.090 --> 00:46:36.750
Well? Does it look good on me?

00:46:40.930 --> 00:46:43.100
Huh?! It looks like you wanna say something!

00:46:43.100 --> 00:46:44.860
N-No, I don't!

00:46:44.860 --> 00:46:48.370
Oh! Fallen for <i>Sonoko-san,</i> have you?!

00:46:48.370 --> 00:46:49.770
Are you serious, Conan?!

00:46:49.770 --> 00:46:51.760
I-It's not like that ...

00:46:55.440 --> 00:46:57.770
Maybe I should try that, too ...

00:47:04.850 --> 00:47:07.420
Inspector! We should go to the party, too!

00:47:07.420 --> 00:47:14.290
No! Seeing as <i>Tokiwa-san</i> said no,
all we can do is wait here!

00:47:14.290 --> 00:47:17.630
All we can do now is pray nothing happens ...

00:47:26.940 --> 00:47:30.210
Wow! Caviar, <i>foie gras,</i> duck!

00:47:30.210 --> 00:47:32.480
This is too much!

00:47:32.480 --> 00:47:36.350
- I think I'll have some, too!
- No. You'll have Japanese food.

00:47:36.350 --> 00:47:39.340
I'll get you some low-calorie dishes.

00:47:40.950 --> 00:47:43.460
She acts like a wife ...

00:47:43.460 --> 00:47:46.030
I'm always starving because of her.

00:47:46.030 --> 00:47:48.860
This car's so cool!

00:47:48.860 --> 00:47:51.500
It's a Ford Mustang convertible!

00:47:51.500 --> 00:47:54.870
But how'd they get something so big in here?

00:47:54.870 --> 00:47:58.870
They probably put it together in here.

00:47:58.870 --> 00:48:02.010
No, they used a freight elevator.

00:48:02.010 --> 00:48:04.340
Freight elevator?

00:48:04.340 --> 00:48:06.380
We have one in our apartment building!

00:48:06.380 --> 00:48:09.120
It's bigger than normal ones,
so dressers are easy to handle!

00:48:09.120 --> 00:48:11.890
Could it hold an elephant too, then?!

00:48:11.890 --> 00:48:14.050
I think so ...

00:48:14.050 --> 00:48:17.050
I don't think anyone has a pet elephant.

00:48:24.160 --> 00:48:27.070
It's so pretty!

00:48:27.070 --> 00:48:30.300
"If Shinichi were here to see
this beautiful view with me,

00:48:30.300 --> 00:48:32.870
I'd be in such bliss!"

00:48:32.870 --> 00:48:34.010
Right?

00:48:34.010 --> 00:48:36.380
Oh, whatever.

00:48:36.380 --> 00:48:40.280
I had wanted Mt. Fuji to be
viewable from that building too,

00:48:40.280 --> 00:48:43.980
but the constituents wouldn't allow it.

00:48:43.980 --> 00:48:47.650
Oh, right. You can't see Mt. Fuji from Tower B.

00:48:53.090 --> 00:49:00.030
Thank you all for attending this,
the grand opening party

00:49:00.030 --> 00:49:02.170
of the Twin Tower Building!

00:49:02.170 --> 00:49:05.940
I would like to start
things off with a little game.

00:49:05.940 --> 00:49:09.980
A game that takes after the name
of my late father Tokiwa Kanenari

00:49:09.980 --> 00:49:14.080
and the 30 years of the Tokiwa Group!

00:49:14.080 --> 00:49:17.920
A 30-second guessing game!

00:49:17.920 --> 00:49:20.590
Just like the one you thought up!

00:49:20.590 --> 00:49:25.060
Whoever counts 30 seconds
exactly or gets the closest

00:49:25.060 --> 00:49:32.670
will receive the Mustang
convertible on display there!

00:49:32.670 --> 00:49:35.030
- Awesome!
- A car!

00:49:35.030 --> 00:49:39.370
- It's a foreign convertible!
- That's so cool!

00:49:39.370 --> 00:49:44.110
However, if there are two winners,
rock-paper-scissors will take place,

00:49:44.110 --> 00:49:50.680
and the loser will have to
tolerate a mountain bike and a helmet!

00:49:50.680 --> 00:49:53.690
- I'd rather have the mountain bike!
- Me too!

00:49:53.690 --> 00:49:56.260
We can't drive cars!

00:49:56.260 --> 00:50:01.030
- Alright, Mitsuhiko!
- We have <i>Ayumi-chan</i> with us!

00:50:01.030 --> 00:50:03.630
Victory is as good as ours!

00:50:03.630 --> 00:50:06.300
Where could <i>Conan-kun</i> be?

00:50:06.300 --> 00:50:10.970
I ask those of you playing the game
to let us hold on to your watches.

00:50:10.970 --> 00:50:16.980
They'll be returned shortly with
gems that suit them perfectly!

00:50:16.980 --> 00:50:20.650
Wow! Gems!

00:50:20.650 --> 00:50:23.420
The Tokiwa zaibatsu doesn't mess around ...

00:50:23.420 --> 00:50:26.120
Here we are!

00:50:26.120 --> 00:50:28.350
Take a flag if you put one in!

00:50:28.350 --> 00:50:29.690
Here you are!

00:50:32.330 --> 00:50:34.430
- Here you are!
- No, I'm okay!

00:50:34.430 --> 00:50:36.130
Same here.

00:50:36.130 --> 00:50:40.270
I have no watch, nor any desire to play games.

00:50:40.270 --> 00:50:43.930
Now, then! Could the children
please come up to the front!

00:50:49.440 --> 00:50:52.930
Huh? Conan and Haibara aren't playing?

00:50:55.010 --> 00:50:57.180
Now let's begin!

00:50:57.180 --> 00:51:03.160
Once you've counted 30 seconds
from her mark, raise your flag!

00:51:03.160 --> 00:51:05.060
Bring it on!

00:51:05.060 --> 00:51:07.390
Ready... Start!

00:51:13.200 --> 00:51:15.200
- 8. 9. 10.
- 15. 16.

00:51:15.200 --> 00:51:17.200
21. 22. 23.

00:51:17.200 --> 00:51:23.310
- 7. 8. 9.
- 8. 9. 10.
- 6... 7... 8...

00:51:23.310 --> 00:51:28.050
24. 25. 26. 27 ...

00:51:28.050 --> 00:51:30.420
Oh no! I lost count!

00:51:30.420 --> 00:51:31.750
Here!

00:51:31.750 --> 00:51:33.120
- Here!
- Here!

00:51:33.120 --> 00:51:36.560
Uh oh! I'll have to go when someone else does!

00:51:36.560 --> 00:51:37.520
Here!

00:51:37.520 --> 00:51:41.190
- Done!
- That blue flag there!

00:51:41.190 --> 00:51:45.570
Congratulations! You're the grand prize winner!

00:51:45.570 --> 00:51:47.200
Dad!

00:51:47.200 --> 00:51:49.140
Are you serious?!

00:51:49.140 --> 00:51:53.140
It's you, <i>Mori-senpai!</i> Come right up!

00:51:53.140 --> 00:51:55.840
Excuse me!

00:51:55.840 --> 00:51:59.480
Everyone! This is the great
detective, Mori <i>Kogoro-san!</i>

00:51:59.480 --> 00:52:02.250
Could you say a little something?

00:52:02.250 --> 00:52:05.910
Now I can say goodbye to the rental car life!

00:52:07.690 --> 00:52:10.390
Oh, Dad ...

00:52:10.390 --> 00:52:15.130
- I got it wrong ...
- I was still on 25 ...

00:52:15.130 --> 00:52:16.790
I was on 12.

00:52:23.100 --> 00:52:24.640
Great. Then I'd be delighted ...

00:52:24.640 --> 00:52:27.840
Excuse me. <i>Kazama-san,</i> if you would ...

00:52:27.840 --> 00:52:29.170
Excuse me.

00:52:36.450 --> 00:52:40.290
And now, for the works of today's main guest,

00:52:40.290 --> 00:52:49.130
our country's master Japanese-style painter,
Kisaragi <i>Hohsui-sensei!</i>

00:52:49.130 --> 00:52:52.200
<i>Kisaragi-sensei</i> deeply loves Mt. Fuji,

00:52:52.200 --> 00:52:56.670
and has painted its majestic
figure for over 30 years!

00:52:56.670 --> 00:53:00.670
And this time, he's donated his
latest work to celebrate the opening

00:53:00.670 --> 00:53:05.780
of the Twin Tower Building,
owned by his pupil, Tokiwa Mio!

00:53:05.780 --> 00:53:09.440
I present to you, "Mt. Fuji in the Spring Snow"!

00:53:15.460 --> 00:53:16.560
Is that...?!

00:53:16.560 --> 00:53:17.890
What?!

00:53:22.160 --> 00:53:23.490
M-Ma'am!

00:53:26.230 --> 00:53:27.560
Damn!

00:53:29.470 --> 00:53:32.170
Get her down! Lower <i>Mio-kun</i> down!

00:53:32.170 --> 00:53:33.910
And shut the curtains!

00:53:33.910 --> 00:53:35.240
Right!

00:53:47.190 --> 00:53:49.180
It's too late ...

00:53:52.360 --> 00:53:55.190
Piano wire in her pearl necklace?!

00:53:55.190 --> 00:53:59.500
The piano wire leads up there?!

00:53:59.500 --> 00:54:01.200
That's ...

00:54:01.200 --> 00:54:02.840
... an <i>O-choko</i> cup!

00:54:02.840 --> 00:54:04.830
<i>Could it be?! Is this also...?!</i>

00:54:06.470 --> 00:54:08.640
Say what?! Tokiwa <i>Mio-san?!</i>

00:54:08.640 --> 00:54:09.970
- Let's go!
- Yes, sir!

00:54:29.300 --> 00:54:31.660
The picture of Mt. Fuji ...

00:54:31.660 --> 00:54:35.600
You can even see Fuji at night here.

00:54:35.600 --> 00:54:38.740
So this is what she meant?

00:54:38.740 --> 00:54:44.540
Basically, this piano wire hook
was attached to <i>Mio-kun's</i> necklace.

00:54:44.540 --> 00:54:46.580
The wire went over the catwalk,

00:54:46.580 --> 00:54:50.420
so when the painting was lowered,
she was pulled up.

00:54:50.420 --> 00:54:53.590
I see. Who else was on the stage then?

00:54:53.590 --> 00:54:56.290
Just me and <i>Kisaragi-sensei.</i>

00:54:56.290 --> 00:54:58.690
Then please stand where you were.

00:54:58.690 --> 00:55:00.560
<i>Chiba-kun,</i> you stand where <i>Tokiwa-san</i> was.

00:55:00.560 --> 00:55:01.530
Yes, Sir.

00:55:01.530 --> 00:55:04.860
These lights were our markers.
The middle was <i>Mio-san's.</i>

00:55:06.700 --> 00:55:08.800
I was over here.

00:55:08.800 --> 00:55:11.800
Meanwhile, you were in the
stage wing, <i>Sawaguchi-san?</i>

00:55:11.800 --> 00:55:15.980
Yes. I was in charge of lowering
and raising the painting ...

00:55:15.980 --> 00:55:17.980
And the pearl necklace?

00:55:17.980 --> 00:55:22.820
She said it was a present from someone,
but I don't know who ...

00:55:22.820 --> 00:55:24.750
When was this picture brought here?

00:55:24.750 --> 00:55:30.390
Last night. I brought it in here in
the presence of <i>Kisaragi-sensei.</i>

00:55:30.390 --> 00:55:34.630
Meaning the piano wire
would've been most easily set by ...

00:55:34.630 --> 00:55:36.630
I'm afraid I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:55:36.630 --> 00:55:39.030
Come to think of it, <i>Kisaragi-san.</i>

00:55:39.030 --> 00:55:42.300
I hear you were mad that
<i>Mio-kun</i> bought all your paintings up

00:55:42.300 --> 00:55:44.840
and then sold them at high prices.

00:55:44.840 --> 00:55:48.910
I hardly think that would be
cause to murder someone!

00:55:48.910 --> 00:55:55.920
But, from what you said earlier,
this appears to be a serial murder...

00:55:55.920 --> 00:56:04.060
If so, seeing as I have an alibi
for the second murder, it can't be me.

00:56:04.060 --> 00:56:07.660
We never showed
<i>Kisaragi-san</i> the last two <i>O-choko</i> cups,

00:56:07.660 --> 00:56:11.660
so he couldn't have known to
leave a similar one here to fool us.

00:56:11.660 --> 00:56:13.500
Umm ...

00:56:13.500 --> 00:56:14.870
Just after the lights went out,

00:56:14.870 --> 00:56:19.410
I did sense someone approach
<i>Mio-san</i> and say something.

00:56:19.410 --> 00:56:22.740
- Really?!
- Was it a man or a woman?!

00:56:22.740 --> 00:56:26.380
I did get a quick whiff of perfume ...

00:56:26.380 --> 00:56:28.610
Yes! I was the one who talked to her!

00:56:28.610 --> 00:56:33.450
But I only went to
double-check things with her ...

00:56:33.450 --> 00:56:34.520
Aha!

00:56:34.520 --> 00:56:37.360
Inspector! I know who did it!

00:56:37.360 --> 00:56:39.530
Eh?!

00:56:39.530 --> 00:56:44.700
The killer is you, Sawaguchi <i>Chinami-san!</i>

00:56:44.700 --> 00:56:47.530
N-No! How can you say that?!

00:56:47.530 --> 00:56:49.370
<i>Sawaguchi-san.</i>

00:56:49.370 --> 00:56:53.440
I'm told your father was a reporter
with a strong sense of justice,

00:56:53.440 --> 00:56:58.080
and that he was always chasing
after <i>politicians</i> wrong doings.

00:56:58.080 --> 00:57:01.450
After he died, you went to work for Tokiwa,

00:57:01.450 --> 00:57:03.450
and became the president's secretary.

00:57:03.450 --> 00:57:06.520
However, during the construction
of the Twin Tower Building,

00:57:06.520 --> 00:57:09.020
wrongdoings took place.

00:57:09.020 --> 00:57:13.530
<i>Mio-kun</i> and <i>Hara-san</i> got together,
handed Councilman Oki money,

00:57:13.530 --> 00:57:17.560
and asked him to revise
the city building ordinance.

00:57:17.560 --> 00:57:21.900
Having inherited your father's
character, you couldn't forgive that.

00:57:21.900 --> 00:57:24.740
So you killed all three of them!

00:57:24.740 --> 00:57:27.740
N-No!

00:57:27.740 --> 00:57:29.440
But, <i>Mori-kun.</i>

00:57:29.440 --> 00:57:32.450
I thought there weren't
any connections between her

00:57:32.450 --> 00:57:35.510
and the <i>O-choko</i> cups left at each crime?

00:57:35.510 --> 00:57:40.420
No, Inspector! <i>"O-choko"</i> is
written as "mouth of the boar"!

00:57:40.420 --> 00:57:44.420
<i>Sawaguchi-san</i> was born
in the year of the "boar,"

00:57:44.420 --> 00:57:47.860
and has "mouth" in her name!

00:57:47.860 --> 00:57:54.870
In short, she left the shattered
<i>O-choko</i> cups at the scenes as messages

00:57:54.870 --> 00:57:59.110
of the crushing anger she
inherited from her father!

00:57:59.110 --> 00:58:01.840
Oh! Brilliant!

00:58:01.840 --> 00:58:04.330
It all fits, and you're not even asleep!

00:58:07.450 --> 00:58:12.720
That's nothing but a
skillfully-forced interpretation.

00:58:12.720 --> 00:58:13.850
Say what?!

00:58:13.850 --> 00:58:17.120
After all, this latest <i>O-choko</i> wasn't shattered!

00:58:17.120 --> 00:58:19.460
If she wanted to express her crushing anger ...

00:58:19.460 --> 00:58:22.120
Shut up, you!

00:58:24.960 --> 00:58:26.500
Oww!

00:58:26.500 --> 00:58:28.500
You seem to be having a hard time.

00:58:28.500 --> 00:58:30.970
If you know something, say so!

00:58:30.970 --> 00:58:32.570
I don't know.

00:58:32.570 --> 00:58:37.480
All I can say is that <i>Mio-san</i>
must've been very drunk at the time.

00:58:37.480 --> 00:58:38.910
Eh?

00:58:38.910 --> 00:58:42.250
Otherwise, don't you think she
would've noticed when the piano wire

00:58:42.250 --> 00:58:44.910
was hooked to her necklace?

00:58:50.160 --> 00:58:55.090
A pearl! What's it doing here?!

00:58:55.090 --> 00:58:58.030
Wait a minute! Could it be...?!

00:58:58.030 --> 00:59:01.170
<i>Kazama-san!</i> I didn't do anything! Right?!

00:59:01.170 --> 00:59:04.770
No, it was too dark to see anything ...

00:59:04.770 --> 00:59:07.430
If that person is the killer, then ...

00:59:23.120 --> 00:59:27.560
Now I see! This was the motive!

00:59:27.560 --> 00:59:30.220
But, if so, then that incident ...

00:59:38.870 --> 00:59:44.610
Ah! So that's what that meant!

00:59:44.610 --> 00:59:46.550
I've figured it all out!

00:59:46.550 --> 00:59:50.040
The whole picture of all
three mysterious incidents!

01:00:10.970 --> 01:00:12.960
W-What's that?!

01:00:21.750 --> 01:00:24.920
- What's this shaking?!
- An earthquake?

01:00:24.920 --> 01:00:27.920
What on earth is happening?!

01:00:27.920 --> 01:00:29.720
- Explosions?!
- What?!

01:00:29.720 --> 01:00:30.620
Where at?!

01:00:30.620 --> 01:00:35.690
The B4 electric room and
the 40th floor computer room!

01:00:35.690 --> 01:00:38.100
- The computer room?!
- Eh?!

01:00:38.100 --> 01:00:41.730
<i>Kazama-san!</i> Tokiwa's main computer is in there!

01:00:41.730 --> 01:00:44.140
All our essential data will be destroyed!

01:00:44.140 --> 01:00:47.040
A fire has also broken out
from the rear of the 40th floor!

01:00:47.040 --> 01:00:49.610
Please evacuate the building immediately!

01:00:49.610 --> 01:00:50.980
Right!

01:00:50.980 --> 01:00:54.350
Inspector! It sounds like
we should evacuate at once!

01:00:54.350 --> 01:00:59.190
If the electric room's blown up,
emergency power's been cut too!

01:00:59.190 --> 01:01:01.650
Then the elevators don't work, either?!

01:01:01.650 --> 01:01:02.890
No.

01:01:02.890 --> 01:01:06.730
Wait! The observation elevator might work!

01:01:06.730 --> 01:01:07.890
Really?!

01:01:07.890 --> 01:01:10.890
It has a different power source
in case VIPs need to evacuate!

01:01:14.830 --> 01:01:16.640
It works!

01:01:16.640 --> 01:01:19.100
- What's the maximum occupancy?
- 9 adults.

01:01:19.100 --> 01:01:21.740
It'll take too long to get everyone out!

01:01:21.740 --> 01:01:23.840
Are there any other escape routes?!

01:01:23.840 --> 01:01:26.180
If you take the emergency
stairs down to the 60th floor,

01:01:26.180 --> 01:01:29.380
you can cross the bridge to get into Tower B!

01:01:29.380 --> 01:01:33.790
Okay! The women, children, and
elderly will take the elevator down!

01:01:33.790 --> 01:01:36.780
Everyone else will take the emergency stairs!

01:02:00.450 --> 01:02:01.850
What's the situation?!

01:02:01.850 --> 01:02:06.820
The electric room exploded, and
the sprinklers and such don't work!

01:02:06.820 --> 01:02:09.050
- The fire doors?!
- Closed!

01:02:09.050 --> 01:02:12.020
Can we get to that bridge from Tower B?!

01:02:12.020 --> 01:02:13.430
There's a direct elevator!

01:02:13.430 --> 01:02:17.260
Alright! Teams A and B to the electric room!

01:02:17.260 --> 01:02:20.230
Team C and I will cross the
bridge from the other building

01:02:20.230 --> 01:02:21.700
and go to the 40th floor!

01:02:21.700 --> 01:02:23.030
Yes, sir!

01:02:25.700 --> 01:02:27.310
Go on, <i>Conan-kun!</i>

01:02:27.310 --> 01:02:29.340
You get on first, <i>Ran-neechan.</i>

01:02:29.340 --> 01:02:30.670
Just go!

01:02:34.010 --> 01:02:35.850
Over the weight limit!

01:02:35.850 --> 01:02:36.880
<i>Conan-kun!</i>

01:02:36.880 --> 01:02:39.750
I'll be fine! I'll take the next one!

01:02:39.750 --> 01:02:41.740
Please go now!

01:02:43.320 --> 01:02:47.230
The remaining women,
<i>Conan-kun,</i> and <i>Kisaragi-san</i>

01:02:47.230 --> 01:02:49.260
will take the next elevator down!

01:02:49.260 --> 01:02:52.730
I will take the stairs.

01:02:52.730 --> 01:02:55.870
But, aren't you?

01:02:55.870 --> 01:02:57.940
Don't treat me like a senior citizen!

01:02:57.940 --> 01:03:00.740
Right! As you wish!

01:03:00.740 --> 01:03:03.240
Alright, <i>Kazama-san.</i> Please go ahead.

01:03:03.240 --> 01:03:09.380
Alright, everyone! I'll lead the way!
Please follow me!

01:03:09.380 --> 01:03:14.050
<i>Shiratori-kun,</i> you guys go, too.
I'll catch up with you later.

01:03:14.050 --> 01:03:15.750
All right!

01:03:15.750 --> 01:03:17.750
Doc, I hate to ask, but ...

01:03:19.020 --> 01:03:20.690
Alright. Got it.

01:03:24.860 --> 01:03:26.190
Huh?

01:03:28.930 --> 01:03:30.270
I'm sorry!

01:03:32.910 --> 01:03:34.810
- Go ahead!
- But ...

01:03:34.810 --> 01:03:36.110
We'll be fine!

01:03:36.110 --> 01:03:40.780
We'll use the bridge on the 60th
floor to go to the next building!

01:03:40.780 --> 01:03:43.520
See you at the bottom!

01:03:43.520 --> 01:03:46.520
Go on, now!

01:03:46.520 --> 01:03:47.850
Thank you, children!

01:03:51.560 --> 01:03:55.230
Oh no! It's pitch dark!
I can't tell where anything is!

01:03:55.230 --> 01:04:00.430
Hey! Now what? We gave
them our Wristwatch Lights earlier ...

01:04:00.430 --> 01:04:04.000
Oh! This is bad!

01:04:04.000 --> 01:04:08.410
Honestly, now. You should've
thought of that before getting off.

01:04:08.410 --> 01:04:12.910
Oh, yeah! You and <i>Conan-kun</i>
didn't participate in the game!

01:04:12.910 --> 01:04:14.550
Let's hurry, then!

01:04:14.550 --> 01:04:19.250
Hold on. Can't we just
wait for the next elevator?

01:04:19.250 --> 01:04:22.820
You're so dumb. The next one will be full, too.

01:04:22.820 --> 01:04:25.480
In any case, let's hurry to the 60th floor!

01:04:54.450 --> 01:04:55.780
Here we go!

01:05:06.470 --> 01:05:09.870
The scale and timing of
these explosions were planned.

01:05:09.870 --> 01:05:14.870
Could the men in black
have planted the bombs?!

01:05:14.870 --> 01:05:19.280
If so, I can imagine why they
blew up the computer room ...

01:05:19.280 --> 01:05:20.610
But why the electric room?

01:05:23.350 --> 01:05:24.680
Get on, please!

01:05:26.920 --> 01:05:30.560
You, too, <i>Chinami-san.</i>
We can talk in detail later.

01:05:30.560 --> 01:05:31.890
All right.

01:05:48.570 --> 01:05:53.580
To keep the sprinklers from
activating? Or some other purpose?

01:05:53.580 --> 01:05:58.080
Good thing this elevator
has its own power source!

01:05:58.080 --> 01:06:01.420
Otherwise, we'd have to
go down all those stairs!

01:06:03.420 --> 01:06:04.750
C-Could it be?!

01:06:13.930 --> 01:06:15.260
Gin!

01:06:31.380 --> 01:06:34.880
Rest in peace, Sherry!

01:06:37.720 --> 01:06:40.210
<i>Sonoko-neechan!</i> Your panties are showing!

01:06:46.270 --> 01:06:49.100
What?! What?! Why are we stopped?!

01:06:52.270 --> 01:06:55.270
It's someone else?

01:06:55.270 --> 01:06:59.610
The laser point is gone!
Did he realize it's the wrong person?!

01:07:12.720 --> 01:07:14.660
It's no use! It won't move!

01:07:14.660 --> 01:07:16.990
- <i>Ran-neechan!</i> Lift me on your shoulders!
- Eh?! Right!

01:07:27.610 --> 01:07:29.270
There you go!

01:07:31.780 --> 01:07:33.770
<i>Conan-kun!</i> Let me do it!

01:07:39.750 --> 01:07:41.690
You can do it, <i>Ran-neechan!</i>

01:07:41.690 --> 01:07:43.020
Please!

01:07:48.030 --> 01:07:49.360
Way to go, Ran!

01:08:03.240 --> 01:08:06.780
- What floor is this?
- The 45th.

01:08:06.780 --> 01:08:09.410
This floor has a bridge!

01:08:09.410 --> 01:08:11.080
Oh no! Smoke!

01:08:13.390 --> 01:08:16.220
Let's run across the bridge
to the next building!

01:08:22.090 --> 01:08:24.090
It's me. Any luck there?

01:08:26.100 --> 01:08:29.090
No, only the men are coming across.

01:08:32.540 --> 01:08:36.140
She probably stayed up above
after realizing what we're after,

01:08:36.140 --> 01:08:39.180
but she won't get away.

01:08:39.180 --> 01:08:41.110
Drop the bridges!

01:08:41.110 --> 01:08:44.110
Everyone! We can cross to
the next building from here!

01:08:53.130 --> 01:08:55.460
Look! There's the bridge!

01:09:05.470 --> 01:09:07.460
Look out, <i>Conan-kun!</i>

01:09:20.250 --> 01:09:24.120
- What happened?!
- The bridges just fell!

01:09:24.120 --> 01:09:26.730
<i>Mori-san!</i> The observation elevator is stopped!

01:09:26.730 --> 01:09:28.060
What?!

01:09:30.130 --> 01:09:31.460
Ran!

01:09:39.600 --> 01:09:42.670
Ran! Are you alright?!

01:09:42.670 --> 01:09:46.480
We're okay!

01:09:46.480 --> 01:09:48.380
What do we do now, <i>Conan-kun?</i>

01:09:48.380 --> 01:09:51.150
This is bad! Our escape routes are cut off!

01:09:51.150 --> 01:09:51.820
Eh?!

01:09:51.820 --> 01:09:53.810
The other side of the fire
door is filled with smoke!

01:09:58.290 --> 01:09:59.280
No ...

01:10:05.160 --> 01:10:06.490
Now what?

01:10:08.330 --> 01:10:10.300
The battery ran out.

01:10:10.300 --> 01:10:14.300
It's dangerous to move about recklessly.
Let's wait here for help.

01:10:18.180 --> 01:10:19.670
Are you all right, <i>Conan-kun?</i>

01:10:34.290 --> 01:10:36.280
<i>Ran-neechan!</i> You're not thinking of?!

01:10:37.460 --> 01:10:40.450
I don't know if it'll work
like in the movies, but ...

01:10:42.670 --> 01:10:44.660
Hold on tight, <i>Conan-kun!</i>

01:10:53.210 --> 01:10:54.680
Oh! It's <i>Ran-san!</i>

01:10:54.680 --> 01:10:56.670
What?! Gimme those!

01:10:59.950 --> 01:11:02.280
W-What is she planning to do?!

01:11:16.400 --> 01:11:19.640
<i>Ran-neechan,</i> you're not scared?

01:11:19.640 --> 01:11:21.670
I'm scared!

01:11:21.670 --> 01:11:27.670
But you're with me,
and Shinichi told me to wait for him ...

01:11:30.280 --> 01:11:32.940
I have to live so I can wait for him ...

01:11:37.920 --> 01:11:42.360
<i>Conan-kun,</i> I'm ...

01:11:42.360 --> 01:11:45.700
It'll be okay, <i>Ran-neechan!</i>

01:11:45.700 --> 01:11:49.030
I know how you feel, so much that it hurts ...

01:12:25.470 --> 01:12:27.460
Oh no! The hose is on fire!

01:12:46.530 --> 01:12:48.690
Are you okay, <i>Conan-kun?!</i>

01:12:48.690 --> 01:12:51.690
Y-Yeah! You're awesome, <i>Ran-neechan!</i>

01:12:56.330 --> 01:12:57.500
<i>Mori-san!</i>

01:13:01.340 --> 01:13:02.670
Ran!

01:13:03.640 --> 01:13:06.340
- Sonoko!
- Thank goodness you're alright!

01:13:06.340 --> 01:13:08.340
Geez! Just had to act crazy!

01:13:13.750 --> 01:13:15.080
Look out!

01:13:18.020 --> 01:13:20.010
Look! The observation elevator!

01:13:25.700 --> 01:13:27.630
Doc! Where is that person?!

01:13:27.630 --> 01:13:31.370
Eh? Oh, sorry! I lost sight of them!

01:13:31.370 --> 01:13:34.370
And I don't see the children, either!

01:13:34.370 --> 01:13:35.700
What?!

01:13:36.710 --> 01:13:39.370
Ayumi! Genta! Mitsuhiko! Do you read me?!

01:13:41.380 --> 01:13:43.450
We read you, <i>Conan-kun!</i>

01:13:43.450 --> 01:13:45.420
Where are you?!

01:13:45.420 --> 01:13:49.490
Actually, right in front
of the 60th floor bridge ...

01:13:49.490 --> 01:13:50.820
What?!

01:13:52.990 --> 01:13:55.060
They're up there?!

01:13:55.060 --> 01:13:57.560
<i>Takagi-kun!</i> Call an emergency helicopter!

01:13:57.560 --> 01:13:58.890
Y-Yes, sir!

01:14:21.890 --> 01:14:23.560
Mister! I'm borrowing your flashlight!

01:14:23.560 --> 01:14:24.890
Little boy! Stop!

01:14:28.130 --> 01:14:29.160
What the...?!

01:14:29.160 --> 01:14:31.600
- That sound!
- It's his skateboard!

01:14:31.600 --> 01:14:32.930
Conan?!

01:14:46.480 --> 01:14:47.610
Oww!

01:14:47.610 --> 01:14:48.950
You're awesome!

01:14:48.950 --> 01:14:50.480
You're so cool!

01:14:50.480 --> 01:14:52.550
You're our savior!

01:14:52.550 --> 01:14:56.540
Geez! This is no time to be impressed!

01:14:59.020 --> 01:14:59.990
What the...?!

01:14:59.990 --> 01:15:02.560
<i>Conan-kun's</i> skateboard!

01:15:02.560 --> 01:15:05.960
<i>Conan-kun</i> just jumped
across the 60th floor bridge!

01:15:05.960 --> 01:15:07.300
What?!

01:15:09.570 --> 01:15:10.640
Megure!

01:15:10.640 --> 01:15:13.470
Inspector! We're going up to the top!

01:15:13.470 --> 01:15:15.010
Have the chopper land on the roof!

01:15:15.010 --> 01:15:17.000
"We"?! Where are you?!

01:15:24.920 --> 01:15:27.990
Going up 15 floors is tough ...

01:15:27.990 --> 01:15:30.920
Hang in there, <i>Genta-kun!</i> We're almost there!

01:15:30.920 --> 01:15:32.250
Y-Yeah ...

01:15:35.790 --> 01:15:37.730
You guys go on ahead.

01:15:37.730 --> 01:15:40.060
Eh? Where are you going, <i>Conan-kun?</i>

01:15:44.570 --> 01:15:47.230
Hey! Where are you going? Hey!

01:15:48.840 --> 01:15:50.140
What's the deal?

01:15:50.140 --> 01:15:53.280
You know how <i>Conan-kun</i> is!
He must have an idea!

01:15:53.280 --> 01:15:55.610
Let's go on up to the roof!

01:15:57.280 --> 01:15:59.270
L-Let me think for a second!

01:16:11.900 --> 01:16:13.200
Someone's in here!

01:16:13.200 --> 01:16:15.860
The person who murdered <i>Oki-san</i> and <i>Mio-san.</i>

01:16:19.870 --> 01:16:22.970
He decided to kill <i>Mio-san</i> for a certain reason,

01:16:22.970 --> 01:16:25.980
so he gave her a pearl necklace as a present.

01:16:25.980 --> 01:16:28.980
He told her to wear the
necklace at the opening party

01:16:28.980 --> 01:16:32.320
and show the painting he
gave as a gift to her on stage.

01:16:32.320 --> 01:16:34.310
Then the killer is!

01:16:37.760 --> 01:16:40.750
Yes. <i>Mio-san's</i> Japanese painting instructor ...

01:16:43.230 --> 01:16:45.220
... Kisaragi <i>Hohsui-san!</i>

01:16:57.910 --> 01:16:59.740
As I recall, you're ...

01:16:59.740 --> 01:17:03.680
... Edogawa Conan. A detective.

01:17:03.680 --> 01:17:10.260
The necklace you gave <i>Mio-san</i>
was made to come undone easily.

01:17:10.260 --> 01:17:15.630
And you had prepared another necklace.

01:17:15.630 --> 01:17:19.600
During the party, you took that necklace out,

01:17:19.600 --> 01:17:21.600
and hooked it to the piano wire hook

01:17:21.600 --> 01:17:26.670
hanging from the painting of Mt. Fuji
and hidden along a curtain fold.

01:17:26.670 --> 01:17:30.610
Next, using the light on the floor,
you walked up to <i>Mio-san</i>

01:17:30.610 --> 01:17:33.340
and undid her necklace.

01:17:33.340 --> 01:17:38.750
To the flustered <i>Mio-san,</i>
you said, "It's okay. I'll get it for you."

01:17:38.750 --> 01:17:41.850
And then you put the other
necklace around her neck ...

01:17:41.850 --> 01:17:45.620
... the piano wire necklace.

01:17:45.620 --> 01:17:46.290
In other words ...

01:17:46.290 --> 01:17:50.300
The hook wasn't attached to <i>Mio-san's</i> necklace.

01:17:50.300 --> 01:17:54.000
The necklace had a hook on it from the start.

01:17:54.000 --> 01:17:56.970
That's why she never noticed it.

01:17:56.970 --> 01:18:03.910
This pearl I picked up fell off
when you took the first necklace off.

01:18:03.910 --> 01:18:07.310
The <i>O-choko</i> cup on the stage
was purposely left there

01:18:07.310 --> 01:18:09.080
to make it look like a serial murder.

01:18:09.080 --> 01:18:13.650
Hold on. <i>Kisaragi-san</i> has
an alibi for <i>Hara-san's</i> murder.

01:18:13.650 --> 01:18:18.650
Of course he does.
Because someone else murdered <i>Hara-san.</i>

01:18:29.670 --> 01:18:31.700
The fire's reached the 70th floor!

01:18:31.700 --> 01:18:34.040
Come on! Where's that emergency chopper?!

01:18:34.040 --> 01:18:36.070
I'll check, sir!

01:18:36.070 --> 01:18:37.410
<i>Conan-kun ...</i>

01:18:38.710 --> 01:18:41.280
That night, after we left,

01:18:41.280 --> 01:18:45.450
you went to <i>Hara-san's</i> apartment to kill him.

01:18:45.450 --> 01:18:47.350
But ...

01:18:47.350 --> 01:18:51.460
<i>... Hara-san</i> was already dead, shot in the chest.

01:18:51.460 --> 01:18:55.360
Thinking quickly,
you disguised it as a serial murder,

01:18:55.360 --> 01:18:59.000
in order to create an alibi for yourself.

01:18:59.000 --> 01:19:02.430
Because with serial murders,
if you have an alibi for one incident,

01:19:02.430 --> 01:19:05.040
you're no longer a suspect.

01:19:05.040 --> 01:19:10.240
So you broke your <i>O-choko</i> cup there,
just like with <i>Oki-san.</i>

01:19:10.240 --> 01:19:14.710
When you did, some of the
fragments fell on the dried blood.

01:19:14.710 --> 01:19:20.950
That's why none of the fragments
in <i>Tome-san's</i> bag had blood.

01:19:20.950 --> 01:19:25.360
And, in the photo from the scene
of <i>Oki-san's</i> murder in the hotel,

01:19:25.360 --> 01:19:29.190
only the lower part of the
closet was covered in blood.

01:19:29.190 --> 01:19:34.200
It was probably because a wall scroll
you painted was hanging there.

01:19:34.200 --> 01:19:39.340
You gave <i>Oki-san</i> that wall scroll
as a pretense to visit his room

01:19:39.340 --> 01:19:41.740
and catch him off guard.

01:19:41.740 --> 01:19:45.780
That's quite the interesting theory,
little detective.

01:19:45.780 --> 01:19:47.780
But your theory has no ...

01:19:47.780 --> 01:19:50.770
I do have proof. Right inside that cane.

01:19:54.790 --> 01:19:59.280
The first necklace <i>Mio-san</i> was
wearing should be hidden inside!

01:20:12.400 --> 01:20:16.470
How did you know I hid it in here?

01:20:16.470 --> 01:20:17.840
The sound.

01:20:17.840 --> 01:20:23.510
The sound of the cane slightly
differed before and after <i>Mio-san</i> died.

01:20:23.510 --> 01:20:25.510
Truly the ears of a detective.

01:20:31.390 --> 01:20:33.380
Oh! Here it comes!

01:20:41.400 --> 01:20:43.270
But what was his motive?

01:20:43.270 --> 01:20:46.870
Because <i>Mio-san</i> bought all his
paintings and sold them for a lot?

01:20:46.870 --> 01:20:51.980
No. His motive was most
likely the Twin Tower Building.

01:20:51.980 --> 01:20:56.850
As for the reason you killed
<i>Oki-san</i> and tried to kill <i>Hara-san ...</i>

01:20:56.850 --> 01:21:00.320
At some point, all of your Mt. Fuji paintings

01:21:00.320 --> 01:21:03.890
were of the same angle and composition.

01:21:03.890 --> 01:21:06.490
You painted them from the same location, yes?

01:21:09.830 --> 01:21:15.500
From a small hill I found on
the outskirts of West Tama City.

01:21:15.500 --> 01:21:20.840
For decades, I visited
that hill to do my paintings.

01:21:20.840 --> 01:21:26.040
But as I grew older, climbing
the hill became more difficult.

01:21:26.040 --> 01:21:31.980
So, three years ago, I bought the
entire hill and built a house there

01:21:31.980 --> 01:21:35.190
so I could paint Mt. Fuji
for the rest of my life.

01:21:35.190 --> 01:21:40.990
I built my workroom in the very best spot.

01:21:40.990 --> 01:21:48.170
From that window,
I had a grand view of Mt. Fuji.

01:21:48.170 --> 01:21:51.500
And then that woman destroyed it!

01:22:01.480 --> 01:22:06.880
Then, does that mean those
broken cups represented Mt. Fuji?

01:22:06.880 --> 01:22:08.890
Yeah. They were his messages of anger

01:22:08.890 --> 01:22:13.020
that the Twin Tower Building
had split Mt. Fuji in two.

01:22:13.020 --> 01:22:17.360
But the cup wasn't broken
when <i>Mio-san</i> was killed!

01:22:17.360 --> 01:22:20.930
That was left to make it
look like a serial murder,

01:22:20.930 --> 01:22:23.900
and there was no reason
to leave the message there.

01:22:23.900 --> 01:22:29.040
Because <i>Mio-san</i> had already
split the painting of Mt. Fuji in two.

01:22:29.040 --> 01:22:32.180
Seeing as the necklace
evidence has been discovered,

01:22:32.180 --> 01:22:35.170
I won't be able to talk my way out of this.

01:22:49.230 --> 01:22:53.560
Sorry. As a detective, I can't allow you to die.

01:22:57.070 --> 01:23:00.060
Hey! Down here!

01:23:01.010 --> 01:23:05.540
How did you figure out
Kisaragi Hohsui's motive?

01:23:05.540 --> 01:23:09.610
It'd been bugging me ever
since we went to his house.

01:23:09.610 --> 01:23:11.980
When we arrived at Asahino Station,

01:23:11.980 --> 01:23:16.390
I saw the Twin Tower Building
split Mt. Fuji behind Mitsuhiko.

01:23:16.390 --> 01:23:20.390
And <i>Kisaragi-san's</i> house was
in the exact opposite direction.

01:23:20.390 --> 01:23:25.560
But the large window in his
workroom was covered by curtains.

01:23:25.560 --> 01:23:32.000
So he didn't want people to see
his view of Mt. Fuji was obstructed ...

01:23:32.000 --> 01:23:36.110
- But there's one other thing.
- <i>Hara-san's</i> killer, right?

01:23:36.110 --> 01:23:41.210
This is only conjecture,
but he was holding a silver knife.

01:23:41.210 --> 01:23:44.750
In Japanese, silver is "gin."

01:23:44.750 --> 01:23:46.250
Look.

01:23:46.250 --> 01:23:51.390
When "gin" is on a liquor bottle,
it's pronounced differently.

01:23:51.390 --> 01:23:52.720
Gin!

01:23:56.660 --> 01:24:00.330
Gin most likely had a gun pointed at <i>Hara-san,</i>

01:24:00.330 --> 01:24:04.170
who quickly picked up a knife on the table.

01:24:04.170 --> 01:24:08.440
Even Gin would've assumed he
was going to use it to put up a fight ...

01:24:08.440 --> 01:24:12.010
... never realizing it was actually a message.

01:24:12.010 --> 01:24:14.150
<i>Hara-san</i> was working with them?

01:24:14.150 --> 01:24:20.480
Yeah. He probably broke into
their computers and stole secret data.

01:24:20.480 --> 01:24:25.020
That's why they killed him,
deleted all of his computer data,

01:24:25.020 --> 01:24:32.400
and blew up the Tokiwa main computer,
where he may have copied it.

01:24:32.400 --> 01:24:36.230
So that's what happened ...

01:24:36.230 --> 01:24:38.700
Oh no! The battery ran out!

01:24:38.700 --> 01:24:42.070
I'll go up and get someone
to help carry <i>Kisaragi-san!</i>

01:24:42.070 --> 01:24:43.560
You wait here!

01:25:13.300 --> 01:25:16.740
- Yay!
- We're saved!

01:25:16.740 --> 01:25:19.730
There's no wind! It should be all right now!

01:25:36.130 --> 01:25:38.460
Come back, guys! Hurry!

01:25:47.510 --> 01:25:49.840
W-Who would do this?!

01:25:52.410 --> 01:25:55.450
That should keep the helicopter away.

01:25:55.450 --> 01:26:01.220
Even if they wait around
for the fire to stop, it'll still be ...

01:26:01.220 --> 01:26:02.550
... time up.

01:26:05.160 --> 01:26:06.490
I'm pooped ...

01:26:10.700 --> 01:26:13.900
What's going on with this building?!

01:26:13.900 --> 01:26:17.400
We'll just have to wait for
the fire on the roof to stop now.

01:26:17.400 --> 01:26:19.730
I don't think we'll have the time for that.

01:26:26.140 --> 01:26:27.470
A bomb?!

01:26:28.580 --> 01:26:31.570
They're under all the tables. The timer is ...

01:26:36.290 --> 01:26:38.460
Only four minutes left!

01:26:38.460 --> 01:26:41.790
Damn! They're going to
blow up the party room last

01:26:41.790 --> 01:26:44.120
so it's not clear who they were after!

01:26:57.210 --> 01:26:58.610
Ran ...

01:26:58.610 --> 01:26:59.940
Hurry!

01:27:09.220 --> 01:27:10.890
Captain! They're not reaching!

01:27:10.890 --> 01:27:13.190
Damn! It's no good!

01:27:13.190 --> 01:27:15.850
Wait a minute! That roof!

01:27:24.940 --> 01:27:26.700
Yes! The key's here!

01:27:26.700 --> 01:27:30.540
I get it! We're going to use this
car to jump to the next building!

01:27:30.540 --> 01:27:32.210
It won't work.

01:27:32.210 --> 01:27:38.550
The buildings are 50 meters apart.
60 if we're jumping across.

01:27:38.550 --> 01:27:41.850
There's a 20 meter height
difference with the other building.

01:27:41.850 --> 01:27:46.820
On Earth, an object can
move horizontally at one speed,

01:27:46.820 --> 01:27:52.660
but due to gravity, it will increase
vertical velocity at a specific rate.

01:27:52.660 --> 01:27:55.970
The equation for a 20-meter fall

01:27:55.970 --> 01:27:59.240
is t equals the square root of 2s over g.

01:27:59.240 --> 01:28:00.840
T being the time,

01:28:00.840 --> 01:28:06.280
g the acceleration due to gravity,
or 9.80665 m/s per second.

01:28:06.280 --> 01:28:08.910
S is the distance fallen: 20 meters.

01:28:08.910 --> 01:28:13.780
Plug these numbers in,
and you get 2.02 seconds.

01:28:13.780 --> 01:28:17.690
In other words, it would take
about 2 seconds to fall 20 meters.

01:28:17.690 --> 01:28:21.460
We have to travel 60 meters
in 2 seconds. Meaning ...

01:28:21.460 --> 01:28:26.430
... 30 meters in 1 second,
or 108 kilometers per hour.

01:28:26.430 --> 01:28:30.940
Given this room's size, we can
get up to 50 or 60 kph at most.

01:28:30.940 --> 01:28:35.870
We'd plummet before
reaching the other building ...

01:28:35.870 --> 01:28:37.710
... but what if we did this?

01:28:37.710 --> 01:28:40.440
Y-You're not thinking of going with the blast?!

01:28:40.440 --> 01:28:43.310
Huh? What?! What're you talking about?!

01:28:43.310 --> 01:28:48.290
<i>Conan-kun</i> is thinking of using the blast
from the explosion to fly further out!

01:28:48.290 --> 01:28:50.390
What?!

01:28:50.390 --> 01:28:53.390
We're gonna die if we wait anyway!

01:28:53.390 --> 01:28:54.720
Let's do it!

01:28:57.760 --> 01:29:00.030
- Let's do it, <i>Conan-kun!</i>
- Let's do it!

01:29:00.030 --> 01:29:01.970
Let's do it super-flashy!

01:29:01.970 --> 01:29:05.300
The key to success will be in the timing.

01:29:05.300 --> 01:29:10.310
The bombs have to go off just as
the car breaks through the window

01:29:10.310 --> 01:29:13.340
or it'll lose speed and plummet straight down.

01:29:13.340 --> 01:29:17.980
Yeah. The problem is you
can't see the timer from the car.

01:29:17.980 --> 01:29:21.590
My watch's battery ran out, too...

01:29:21.590 --> 01:29:23.950
In that case, we have <i>Ayumi-chan!</i>

01:29:23.950 --> 01:29:26.960
She might be able to count 30 seconds exactly!

01:29:26.960 --> 01:29:29.560
But she got it wrong just a while ago ...

01:29:29.560 --> 01:29:31.430
Oh.

01:29:31.430 --> 01:29:33.600
What do you think, <i>Ayumi-chan?</i> Can you do it?

01:29:33.600 --> 01:29:38.400
I-I'm not very confident, but...
if you're with me, Conan-kun...!

01:29:38.400 --> 01:29:39.800
Eh?!

01:29:39.800 --> 01:29:44.340
I think I can do it, if you're by my side!

01:29:44.340 --> 01:29:45.670
Ayumi ...

01:29:49.480 --> 01:29:54.080
In that case, how about I stay by
the timer and count until 30 seconds

01:29:54.080 --> 01:29:57.690
and then get in the car?

01:29:57.690 --> 01:30:00.860
There's no time to think! Let's go with that!

01:30:00.860 --> 01:30:04.660
What?! There are bombs in the party room?!

01:30:04.660 --> 01:30:07.000
Have them open the dome roof right away!

01:30:07.000 --> 01:30:09.730
- The roof?!
- Just hurry!

01:30:09.730 --> 01:30:11.060
<i>Kazama-san!</i>

01:30:13.040 --> 01:30:17.710
Hello?! It's me! Open the dome
roof immediately! Right away!

01:30:17.710 --> 01:30:19.040
Pardon me!

01:30:19.040 --> 01:30:21.910
What are you doing, <i>Conan-kun?!</i>

01:30:21.910 --> 01:30:25.450
<i>Ran-neechan,</i> I'm coming there now.

01:30:25.450 --> 01:30:27.780
- Just hurry!
- Hello?! <i>Conan-kun?!</i>

01:30:35.430 --> 01:30:36.760
Alright!

01:30:52.410 --> 01:30:54.510
55. 54.

01:30:54.510 --> 01:30:56.010
53. 52.

01:30:56.010 --> 01:30:58.420
51. 50.

01:30:58.420 --> 01:30:59.750
49. 48.

01:30:59.750 --> 01:31:02.720
47. 46. 45.

01:31:02.720 --> 01:31:04.620
44. 43.

01:31:04.620 --> 01:31:06.660
42. 41.

01:31:06.660 --> 01:31:09.690
40. 39. 38.

01:31:09.690 --> 01:31:11.630
37. 36.

01:31:11.630 --> 01:31:14.700
35. 34. 33.

01:31:14.700 --> 01:31:16.730
32. 31.

01:31:16.730 --> 01:31:17.740
30!

01:31:17.740 --> 01:31:18.540
29!

01:31:18.540 --> 01:31:19.440
28!

01:31:19.440 --> 01:31:20.570
<i>Haibara-san!</i>

01:31:20.570 --> 01:31:21.640
What's going on?!

01:31:21.640 --> 01:31:24.740
It's <i>Haibara-san!</i> She won't stop counting!

01:31:24.740 --> 01:31:25.740
What?!

01:31:25.740 --> 01:31:28.650
Haibara! What're you doing?! Get over here!

01:31:28.650 --> 01:31:32.050
Don't be dumb. This way is more accurate.

01:31:32.050 --> 01:31:35.520
Don't tell me she's planning to
stay behind and sacrifice herself?!

01:31:35.520 --> 01:31:36.520
21!

01:31:36.520 --> 01:31:37.850
20!

01:31:44.460 --> 01:31:45.230
What are you doing?!

01:31:45.230 --> 01:31:50.500
My mom said it's bad luck to
waste even one grain of rice!

01:31:50.500 --> 01:31:51.640
11!

01:31:51.640 --> 01:31:52.640
10!

01:31:52.640 --> 01:31:53.900
9! 8!

01:31:53.900 --> 01:31:55.470
- Here!
- 7!

01:31:55.470 --> 01:31:57.470
- 6! 5!
- Here we go!

01:31:57.470 --> 01:31:58.480
4!

01:31:58.480 --> 01:31:59.480
3!

01:31:59.480 --> 01:32:00.480
2!

01:32:00.480 --> 01:32:01.050
1!

01:32:01.050 --> 01:32:02.380
0!

01:32:09.790 --> 01:32:11.120
<i>Haibara-san!</i>

01:32:13.760 --> 01:32:16.420
I absolutely won't let go!

01:32:18.560 --> 01:32:21.730
Oh no! At this rate
she'll run into those pillars!

01:32:23.100 --> 01:32:25.090
I'm borrowing this!

01:32:55.170 --> 01:32:56.500
<i>Conan-kun!</i>

01:32:59.270 --> 01:33:00.700
<i>Ran-neechan!</i>

01:33:00.700 --> 01:33:01.870
We're okay!

01:33:01.870 --> 01:33:03.200
Yay!

01:33:06.940 --> 01:33:10.080
Say, <i>Conan-kun!</i> Where did you learn to drive?!

01:33:10.080 --> 01:33:12.070
My old man taught me in Hawaii ...

01:33:20.560 --> 01:33:25.330
Boss, there were five kids
and an old man in the car.

01:33:25.330 --> 01:33:29.700
It appears she never came to the party.

01:33:29.700 --> 01:33:33.570
No matter.
We accomplished our original objective.

01:33:33.570 --> 01:33:38.110
Yes. But to think he'd betray us

01:33:38.110 --> 01:33:42.650
and sneak into the organization's computers ...

01:33:42.650 --> 01:33:44.680
Got it, boss!

01:33:44.680 --> 01:33:48.190
The Twin Tower Building in
West Tama City's where the hacker is!

01:33:48.190 --> 01:33:50.620
It must be Hara's doing after all.

01:33:50.620 --> 01:33:55.590
We took care of Hara,
and blew up Tokiwa's main computer.

01:33:55.590 --> 01:33:58.580
The organization's
information won't leak outside now.

01:34:02.870 --> 01:34:07.940
I had hoped to use that
building as her execution grounds,

01:34:07.940 --> 01:34:09.930
but I'll save that fun for another time.

01:34:28.190 --> 01:34:30.960
I can't believe
<i>Kisaragi-san</i> was behind it all ...

01:34:30.960 --> 01:34:32.660
It's a shock ...

01:34:32.660 --> 01:34:36.930
You think? I suspected him from the very start!

01:34:36.930 --> 01:34:40.000
This is probably as far as
the police will investigate.

01:34:40.000 --> 01:34:45.680
Yeah. They'll likely never find
out Gin murdered <i>Hara-san,</i> either.

01:34:45.680 --> 01:34:48.670
And the truth about the
bombing will remain in the dark ...

01:34:53.650 --> 01:34:58.020
Thank you for earlier. You saved me.

01:34:58.020 --> 01:35:01.730
No, I only did my duty as a man!

01:35:01.730 --> 01:35:05.220
You too, <i>Kojima-kun.</i>
So I'm the same as a grain of rice?

01:35:08.800 --> 01:35:13.440
Still, Ayumi! How did you
get 30 seconds exactly again?!

01:35:13.440 --> 01:35:14.770
Just luck!

01:35:18.440 --> 01:35:22.280
The truth is, it's thanks to you, <i>Conan-kun!</i>

01:35:22.280 --> 01:35:24.680
When you're by my side, I get excited

01:35:24.680 --> 01:35:27.680
and I can count time using my heartbeat!

01:35:27.680 --> 01:35:30.950
Come to think of it, the first
time you counted 30 seconds ...

01:35:30.950 --> 01:35:34.160
28! 29! 30!

01:35:34.160 --> 01:35:37.330
So that's why you wanted me with you ...

01:35:37.330 --> 01:35:39.830
You were so cool, <i>Mitsuhiko-kun!</i>

01:35:39.830 --> 01:35:40.800
Oh, uhh ...

01:35:40.800 --> 01:35:42.200
You too, <i>Genta-kun!</i>

01:35:42.200 --> 01:35:43.300
Yeah?!

01:35:43.300 --> 01:35:47.770
- Hey! What're you gonna do now?
- What do you mean?!

01:35:47.770 --> 01:35:51.480
If you make <i>Yoshida-san</i> cry,
I'll make you regret it!

01:35:51.480 --> 01:35:52.810
Hey, now!

01:36:09.300 --> 01:36:16.940
son janai!? ima kara de mo,  iin janai!? yareru koto

